('758021','UOW','Diploma of Arts, Social Sciences and Humanities – Pathway Courses','Delivered by: a href=\"https://www.uowcollege.edu.au/\" \"noopener noreferrer\" \"_blank\"UOW College AustraliaPathway to: University of Wollongong (UOW) bachelor&#39s degreesThe Diploma of Arts, Social Science and Humanities offers students a supported introduction to university study, helping them build confidence and develop effective learning strategies for success in higher education.In the initial session, students complete tailored subjects designed to strengthen academic skills and prepare them for university-level learning. In sessions 2 and 3, students explore key disciplines such as human geography, history, international relations, public health, and sociology, gaining foundational knowledge and experience in these areas.Graduates of the diploma are eligible for entry into a range of bachelor degrees within the Faculty of Arts, Social Sciences and Humanities at UOW. Depending on the chosen pathway, students may also receive up to 48 credit points towards their degree.','emBachelor of Arts: /emRefer to 753101. emBachelor of Communication and Media: /emRefer to 753110. emBachelor of Creative Arts (Creative Writing): /emRefer to 754601. emBachelor of Creative Arts (Music): /em754603. emBachelor of Creative Arts (Performance and Theatre):/em Refer to 754604. emBachelor of Creative Arts (Visual Arts): /emRefer to 754605.em Bachelor of Creative Arts (Visual Arts and Design): /emRefer to 754607. emBachelor of International Studies: /emRefer to 753121.em Bachelor of Psychological Science - Bachelor of Social Science: /emRefer to 751761. emBachelor of Social Science: /emRefer to 755300. emBachelor of Social Work: /emRefer to 755340.','emDiploma of Arts and Social Sciences: /emHealth and society, history and sociology, human geography, social science. emBachelor of Arts: /emRefer to 753101. emBachelor of Communication and Media: /emRefer to 753110. emBachelor of Creative Arts (Cre