('758031','UOW','Diploma of Business Fast Track – Pathway Courses','Delivered by: a href=\"https://www.uowcollege.edu.au/\" \"noopener noreferrer\" \"_blank\"UOW College AustraliaPathway to: University of Wollongong (UOW) bachelor&#39s degreesspan \"background-(250, 250, 250) (66, 66, 66)\"The Diploma of Business Fast Track offers a supported and accelerated introduction to university study, helping students build confidence and develop effective learning strategies for success in higher education.span \"background-(250, 250, 250) (66, 66, 66)\"Students engage with core business disciplines including marketing, accounting, and management, gaining foundational knowledge and practical experience in these areas. The course is designed to prepare students for the academic demands of a business degree while providing additional support to help them thrive.The Diploma of Business Fast Track provides a direct pathway into the second year of the Bachelor of Business, Bachelor of Business - Bachelor of Laws, or Bachelor of Business Analytics and the first year of a Bachelor of Laws at the University of Wollongong (UOW).','emBachelor of Business:/em Refer to 751237. emBachelor of Business Analytics:/em Refer to 751762. \" background-\"emBachelor of Business - Bachelor of Laws:/emspan \" background-\" Refer to 751251. \" background-\"emBachelor of Laws:/emspan \" background-\" Refer to 756100.','emDiploma of Business: /emConcepts of demand, corporate and personal finance, managing resources, marketing concepts and principles, quantitative techniques, supply and market structures. emBachelor of Business:/em Refer to 751237. emBachelor of Business Analytics:/em Refer to 751762. \"background- \"emBachelor of Business - Bachelor of Laws:/emspan \"background- \" Refer to 751251. \"background- \"emBachelor of Laws:/emspan \"background- \" Refer to 756100.','N/A','https://www.uow.edu.au/student/finances/domestic-undergraduate/contribution/','https://www.uowcollege.edu.au/courses-pathways/#/'),
('758041','UOW','Diploma of Business – Pathway Courses','Delivered by: a href=\"https://www.uowcollege.edu.au/\" \"noopener noreferrer\" \"_blank\"UOW College AustraliaPathway to: University of Wollongong (UOW) bachelor&#39s degreesThe Diploma of Business offers students a supported introduction to university study, helping them build confidence and develop effective learning strategies for success in higher education.In the initial session, students complete tailored subjects designed to strengthen academic skills and prepare them for university-level learning. In sessions 2 and 3, students are provided with a range of experiences and opportunities to engage with key disciplinary areas including marketing, accounting and management, gaining foundational knowledge and experience in these areas.span \"background- (0, 22, 65)\"The Diploma of Business provides a direct pathway into the second year of the Bachelor of Business, Bachelor of Business - Bachelor of Laws, or Bachelor of Business Analytics and the first year of a Bachelor of Laws at the University of Wollongong (UOW). ','emBachelor of Business:/em Refer to 751237. emBachelor of Business Analytics:/em Refer to 751762. emBachelor of Business - Bachelor of Laws:/em Refer to 751251. emBachelor of Laws:/em Refer to 756100.','emDiploma of Business: /emConcepts of demand, corporate and personal finance, managing resources, marketing concepts and principles, quantitative techniques, supply and market structures. emBachelor of Business:/em Refer to 751237. emBachelor of Business Analytics:/em Refer to 751762. emBachelor of Business - Bachelor of Laws:/em Refer to 751251. emBachelor of Laws:/em Refer to 756100.','N/A','https://www.uow.edu.au/student/finances/domestic-undergraduate/contribution/','https://www.uowcollege.edu.au/courses-pathways/#/'),
('758051','UOW','Diploma of Engineering Fast Track/Bachelor of Engineering (Honours) (Flexible First Year)','Delivered by: a href=\"https://www.uowcollege.edu.au/\" \"noopener noreferrer\" \"_blank\"UOW College AustraliaPathway to: University of Wollongong (UOW) Bachelor of Engineering (Honours) (Flexible First Year)The Diploma of Engineering Fast Track provides a supported and accelerated pathway into university study, helping students build confidence and develop effective learning strategies for success in higher education.Students engage with core first-year engineering subjects, combining theoretical knowledge with practical, hands-on experience in key areas such as mathematics and physics. The course also introduces students to a variety of engineering disciplines, laying a strong foundation for future study and career pathways.This fast-tracked option is ideal for students ready to dive into university-level engineering with additional academic support to help them thrive.Successful completion of the diploma provides entry into the second year of the Bachelor of Engineering (Honours) (Flexible First Year) at the University of Wollongong (UOW).','Computer architect, computer systems engineer, civil engineer, construction manager, electronics engineer, electrical engineer, environmental engineer, geotechnical engineer, materials engineer, mechanical engineer, metallurgist, network engineer, production engineer, security engineer, software engineer, structural engineer, systems analyst, telecommunications engineer, transport engineer, water quality manager.','emDiploma of Engineering:/em Foundations and essentials for engineering mathematics, sustainability, mechanics, materials in design, computing, analysis, electrical systems, physics. emBachelor of Engineering (Honours) (Flexible First Year):/em Refer to 755624.','N/A','https://www.uow.edu.au/student/finances/domestic-undergraduate/contribution/','https://www.uowcollege.edu.au/courses-pathways/#/'),
('758053','UOW','Diploma of Engineering/Bachelor of Engineering (Honours) (Flexible First Year)','Delivered by: a href=\"https://www.uowcollege.edu.au/\" \"noopener noreferrer\" \"_blank\"UOW College AustraliaPathway to: University of Wollongong (UOW) Bachelor of Engineering (Honours) (Flexible First Year)The Diploma of Engineering offers a supported pathway into university study, designed to help students build confidence and develop the essential skills needed for success in an engineering degree.In the first phase of the course, students focus on developing effective learning strategies and strengthening foundational mathematical skills critical to engineering. The second phase introduces students to first-year core engineering subjects, delivered with additional academic support to enhance understanding and improve outcomes.Successful completion of the diploma provides entry into the second year of the Bachelor of Engineering (Honours) (Flexible First Year) at the University of Wollongong (UOW).',' Computer architect, computer systems engineer, civil engineer, construction manager, electronics engineer, electrical engineer, environmental engineer, geotechnical engineer, materials engineer, mechanical engineer, metallurgist, network engineer, production engineer, security engineer, software engineer, structural engineer, systems analyst, telecommunications engineer, transport engineer, water quality manager. ','emDiploma of Engineering:/em Foundations and essentials for engineering mathematics, sustainability, mechanics, materials in design, computing, analysis, electrical systems, physics. emBachelor of Engineering (Honours) (Flexible First Year):/em Refer to 755624.','N/A','https://www.uow.edu.au/student/finances/domestic-undergraduate/contribution/','https://www.uowcollege.edu.au/courses-pathways/#/'),
('758061','UOW','Diploma of Information Technology Fast Track – Pathway Courses','Delivered by: a href=\"https://www.uowcollege.edu.au/\" \"noopener noreferrer\" \"_blank\"UOW College AustraliaPathway to: University of Wollongong (UOW) bachelor&#39s degreesThe Diploma of Information Technology Fast Track offers students a supported introduction to university study, helping them build confidence and develop effective learning strategies for success in higher education. Students are provided with a range of experiences and opportunities to engage with key disciplinary areas, including programming, systems analysis and web technology, gaining foundational knowledge and experience in these areas.Successful completion of the diploma provides a pathway into the second year of the Bachelor of Business Information Systems, the Bachelor of Computer Science, and the Bachelor of Information Technology at the University of Wollongong (UOW).','emBachelor of Business Information Systems:/em Refer to 754500. emBachelor of Computer Science: /emRefer to 754100. emBachelor of Information Technology: /emRefer to 754300.','emDiploma of Information Technology: /emConcepts and practice of object-oriented programming fundamental database concepts and skills in the design and manipulation of relational databases major information systems found in a typical business structured programming techniques and technologies of structured systems analysis. emBachelor of Business Information Systems:/em Refer to 754500. emBachelor of Computer Science: /emRefer to 754100. emBachelor of Information Technology: /emRefer to 754300.','N/A','https://www.uow.edu.au/student/finances/domestic-undergraduate/contribution/','https://www.uowcollege.edu.au/courses-pathways/#/'),
('758071','UOW','Diploma of Information Technology – Pathway Courses','Delivered by: a href=\"https://www.uowcollege.edu.au/\" \"noopener noreferrer\" \"_blank\"UOW College AustraliaPathway to: University of Wollongong (UOW) bachelor&#39s degreesThe Diploma of Information Technology offers students a supported introduction to university study, helping them build confidence and develop effective learning strategies for success in higher education.In the initial session, students complete tailored subjects designed to strengthen academic skills and prepare them for university-level learning. In sessions 2 and 3, students are provided with a range of experiences and opportunities to engage with key disciplinary areas including programming, systems analysis and web technology, gaining foundational knowledge and experience in these areas.Successful completion of the diploma provides a pathway into the second year of the Bachelor of Business Information Systems, the Bachelor of Computer Science, and the Bachelor of Information Technology at the University of Wollongong (UOW).','emBachelor of Business Information Systems:/em Refer to 754500. emBachelor of Computer Science: /emRefer to 754100. emBachelor of Information Technology: /emRefer to 754300.','emDiploma of Information Technology: /emConcepts and practice of object-oriented programming fundamental database concepts and skills in the design and manipulation of relational databases major information systems found in a typical business structured programming techniques and technologies of structured systems analysis. emBachelor of Business Information Systems:/em Refer to 754500. emBachelor of Computer Science: /emRefer to 754100. emBachelor of Information Technology: /emRefer to 754300.','N/A','https://www.uow.edu.au/student/finances/domestic-undergraduate/contribution/','https://www.uowcollege.edu.au/courses-pathways/#/'),
('758081','UOW','Diploma of Medical and Health Sciences Fast Track – Pathway Courses','Delivered by: a href=\"https://www.uowcollege.edu.au/\" \"noopener noreferrer\" \"_blank\"UOW College AustraliaPathway to: University of Wollongong (UOW) bachelor&#39s degreesThe Diploma of Medical and Health Sciences Fast Track offers a supported and accelerated pathway into university study, providing students with a strong foundation in chemical and biological sciences. Students gain an understanding of applied sciences, including the anatomical, molecular, and physiological processes that underpin human health and function.Throughout the course, students engage in discipline-based science subjects and gain hands-on experience in UOW’s science laboratories. Dedicated tutorials offer additional academic support to help students succeed.The Diploma of Medical and Health Sciences Fast Track provides a direct pathwayspan \"background- \" into the second year of the Bachelor of Medical and Health Sciences, the Bachelor of Nutrition Science, and the Bachelor of Exercise Science at the University of Wollongong (UOW).','emBachelor of Exercise Science/em: Refer to 757642. emBachelor of Medical and Health Sciences/em: Refer to 757630. emBachelor of Nutrition Science/em: Refer to 757645.','emDiploma of Medical and Health Sciences:/em Applied sciences including anatomical, molecular and physiological process of human health and function chemical and biological sciencesem. Bachelor of Exercise Science/em: Refer to 757642. emBachelor of Medical and Health Sciences/em: Refer to 757630. emBachelor of Nutrition Science/em: Refer to 757645. ','N/A','https://www.uow.edu.au/student/finances/domestic-undergraduate/contribution/','https://www.uowcollege.edu.au/courses-pathways/#/'),
('758086','UOW','Diploma of Medical and Health Sciences – Pathway Courses','Delivered by: a href=\"https://www.uowcollege.edu.au/\" \"noopener noreferrer\" \"_blank\"UOW College AustraliaPathway to: University of Wollongong (UOW) bachelor&#39s degreesThe Diploma of Medical and Health Sciences offers a supported introduction to university study, helping students build confidence and develop effective learning strategies for success in higher education.Students gain a strong foundation in chemical and biological sciences, along with an understanding of applied sciences such as anatomy, molecular biology, and human physiology. In the first session, students complete subjects designed to strengthen academic skills and prepare them for university-level learning. In sessions 2 and 3, students engage in discipline-based science subjects and gain hands-on experience working in UOW’s science laboratories, supported by dedicated tutorials to enhance their success.Successful completion of the diploma provides a direct pathway into the second year of the Bachelor of Medical and Health Sciences, Bachelor of Nutrition Science, and Bachelor of Exercise Science at the University of Wollongong (UOW).','emBachelor of Medical and Health Sciences/em: Refer to 757630. emBachelor of Nutrition Science/em: Refer to 757645. emBachelor of Exercise Science/em: Refer to 757642.','em/ememDiploma of Medical and Health Sciences:/em Applied sciences including anatomical, molecular and physiological process of human health and function chemical and biological sciencesem. Bachelor of Medical and Health Sciences/em: Refer to 757630. emBachelor of Nutrition Science/em: Refer to 757645. emBachelor of Exercise Science/em: Refer to 757642.','N/A','https://www.uow.edu.au/student/finances/domestic-undergraduate/contribution/','https://www.uowcollege.edu.au/courses-pathways/#/'),
('758090','UOW','Diploma of Nursing – HLT54121','Delivered by: a href=\"https://www.uowcollege.edu.au/\" \"noopener noreferrer\" \"_blank\"UOW College Australia (span \"background- (0, 22, 65)\"RTO: 91159)Pathway to: University of Wollongong (UOW) Bachelor of NursingA career in nursing is both rewarding and impactful, offering the opportunity to make a real difference in the lives of individuals, families, and communities. Nurses play a vital role in delivering care across a wide range of health conditions, from acute and chronic to complex needs, within a growing and essential industry.The HLT54121 Diploma of Nursing equips students with the knowledge, skills, and attributes required to become an Enrolled Nurse. Students learn to communicate effectively with patients and healthcare teams, administer and monitor medications, manage wound care, and conduct health assessments and care planning.The Diploma of Nursing provides a direct pathway into the second year of the Bachelor of Nursing at the University of Wollongong.This is a nationally approved vocational course that is recognised throughout Australia.','Enrolled Nurses provide nursing care to patients in a variety of health, aged care, welfare and community settings, in many cases under the supervision of Registered Nurses. ','Nursing for primary, chronic, aged and mental health care, administer medications, wound management, communication skills. ','You will have opportunities to apply theory to practice in modern simulated supported learning environments, prior to undertaking workplace experience. During the course you will 400 hours of clinical work placement experiences with healthcare facilities.','https://www.uow.edu.au/student/finances/domestic-undergraduate/contribution/','https://www.uowcollege.edu.au/courses-pathways/#/'),
('758091','UOW','Diploma of Nursing – HLT54121/Bachelor of Nursing','Delivered by: a href=\"https://www.uowcollege.edu.au/\" \"noopener noreferrer\" \"_blank\"UOW College Australia (span \"background- (0, 22, 65)\"RTO: 91159)Pathway to: University of Wollongong (UOW) Bachelor of NursingAA career in nursing is both rewarding and impactful, offering the opportunity to make a real difference in the lives of individuals, families, and communities. Nurses play a vital role in delivering care across a wide range of health conditions, from acute and chronic to complex needs, within a growing and essential industry.The HLT54121 Diploma of Nursing equips students with the knowledge, skills, and attributes required to become an Enrolled Nurse. Students learn to communicate effectively with patients and healthcare teams, administer and monitor medications, manage wound care, and conduct health assessments and care planning.The Diploma of Nursing provides a direct pathway into the second year of the Bachelor of Nursing at the University of Wollongong.This is a nationally approved vocational course that is recognised throughout Australia.','emDiploma of Nursing: /emEnrolled Nurses provide nursing care to patients in a variety of health, aged care, welfare and community settings, in many cases under the supervision of Registered Nurses. emBachelor of Nursing: /emRefer to 757111. ','emDiploma of Nursing: /em Nursing for primary, chronic, aged and mental health care, administer medications, wound management, communication skills. &nbspemBachelor of Nursing: /emRefer to 757111. ','N/A','https://www.uow.edu.au/student/finances/domestic-undergraduate/contribution/','https://www.uowcollege.edu.au/courses-pathways/#/'),
('758101','UOW','Diploma of Science Fast Track - Pathway Courses','Delivered by: a href=\"https://www.uowcollege.edu.au/\" \"noopener noreferrer\" \"_blank\"UOW College AustraliaPathway to: University of Wollongong (UOW) bachelor&#39s degreesThe Diploma of Science Fast Track offers a supported and accelerated pathway into university study, providing students with hands-on experience and foundational knowledge in key scientific disciplines.Students engage with subjects in biology, chemistry, and earth sciences, gaining practical experience in UOW’s science laboratories. Dedicated support tutorials are provided throughout the course to enhance learning and help students succeed.The Diploma of Science Fast Track provides a direct pathway into the second year of a Bachelor of Science and the Bachelor of Marine Science.','Biological scientist, biochemist, chemist, conservation biologist, ecologist, environmental assessor, geologist, geochemist, population analyst, regional planner.','emDiploma of Science: /emBiodiversity and environment, biological sciences, chemistry, climate change, Earth sciences, mathematics. emBachelor of Marine Science: /emRefer to 757622. emBachelor of Science: /emRefer to 757621. ','N/A','https://www.uow.edu.au/student/finances/domestic-undergraduate/contribution/','https://www.uowcollege.edu.au/courses-pathways/#/'),
('758106','UOW','Diploma of Science - Pathway Courses','Delivered by: a href=\"https://www.uowcollege.edu.au/\" \"noopener noreferrer\" \"_blank\"UOW College AustraliaPathway to: University of Wollongong (UOW) bachelor&#39s degreesThe Diploma of Science offers a supported pathway into university study, helping students build confidence and develop effective learning strategies for success in higher education.In the first session, students complete subjects designed to strengthen academic skills and prepare them for university-level learning. In sessions 2 and 3, students engage with key scientific disciplines including biology, chemistry, and earth sciences, with hands-on experience in UOW’s science laboratories. Dedicated support tutorials are provided throughout to enhance student success.The Diploma of Science provides a direct pathway into the second year of the Bachelor of Science and the Bachelor of Marine Science at the University of Wollongong (UOW).',' Biological scientist, biochemist, chemist, conservation biologist, ecologist, environmental assessor, geologist, geochemist, population analyst, regional planner. ','emDiploma of Science:/em Biodiversity and environment, biological sciences, chemistry, earth sciences, mathematics. emBachelor of Marine Science: /emRefer to 757622. emBachelor of Science: /emRefer to 757621. ','N/A','https://www.uow.edu.au/student/finances/domestic-undergraduate/contribution/','https://www.uowcollege.edu.au/courses-pathways/#/'),
('758114','UOW','University Entrance Program – Pathway Courses','Delivered by: a href=\"https://www.uowcollege.edu.au/\" \"noopener noreferrer\" \"_blank\"UOW College AustraliaPathway to: University of Wollongong (UOW) bachelor&#39s degreesThe University Entrance Program (UEP) is 14-week pathway program for students who do not meet direct entry requirements for a University of Wollongong (UOW) bachelor&#39s degree. It prepares students for university study through academic skill building and tailored support.Students choose from three study streams each aligned with future degree goals. Upon successful completion, students can progress to selected UOW bachelor&#39s degrees.The UEP is offered across multiple UOW campuses, with delivery modes designed to suit each location. Students in Wollongong and Liverpool engage with the UEP through face-to-face learning, while those in Bega Valley, Eurobodalla, and Shoalhaven participate online, with access to dedicated support and resources at their local campuses. Bachelor&#39s degrees are delivered face-to-face at their respective UOW campuses.UEP Stream 1 - Arts, Education, Business, Nursing, Psychology, CriminologyWollongong: Bachelor of Arts (Psychology), Bachelor of Criminology, Bachelor of Education (The Early Years, Primary, Secondary - English, Health and Physical Education, Modern History), Bachelor of Psychological ScienceBega Vally: Bachelor of Arts, Bachelor of NursingEurobodalla: Bachelor of Business, Bachelor of NursingLiverpool: Bachelor of Criminology, Bachelor of Primary EducationShoalhaven: Bachelor of Arts, Bachelor of Business, Bachelor of NursingUEP Stream 2 - Science EducationWollongong: Bachelor of Secondary Education (Biology, Chemistry, Earth and Environmental Science, Physics)UEP Stream 3 - Mathematics and ScienceWollongong: Bachelor of Mathematics, Bachelor of Science (EIS), Bachelor of Secondary Education (Mathematics)','emBachelor of Arts:/em Refer to 753101. emBachelor of Arts (Psychology):/em Refer to 753200. emBachelor of Criminology: /emRefer to 753125. emBachelor Education (The Early Years):/em Refer to 755113. emBachelor of Nursing:/em Refer to 757101. emBachelor of Primary Education:/em Refer to 755112. emBachelor of Psychological Science:/em Refer to 753220. emBachelor of Secondary Education (Health and Physical Education):/em Refer to 755101. emBachelor of Secondary Education (Biology, Chemistry, Earth and Environmental Science, or Physics):/em Refer to 755104-755107. emBachelor of Mathematics:/em Refer to 756511. emBachelor of Science (EIS):/em Refer to 757633, 757634, 757637. emBachelor of Secondary Education (Mathematics):/em Refer to 755102.','emUniversity Entrance Program:/em Language, mathematics, science.em Bachelor of Arts:/em Refer to 753101. emBachelor of Arts (Psychology)/em: Refer to 753200.em Bachelor of Criminology: /emRefer to 753125.em Bachelor Education (The Early Years)/em: Refer to 755113. emBachelor of Nursing:/em Refer to 757101. emBachelor of Primary Education:/em Refer to 755112. emBachelor of Psychological Science:/em Refer to 753220. emBachelor of Secondary Education (English):/em Refer to 755108. emBachelor of Secondary Education (Health and Physical Education):/em Refer to 755101. emBachelor of Secondary Education (Modern History):/em Refer to 755109.em Bachelor of Secondary Education (Biology, Chemistry, Earth and Environmental Science, or Physics):/em Refer to 755104-755107.em Bachelor of Mathematics: /emRefer to 756511. emBachelor of Science (EIS):/em Refer to 757633, 757634, 757637. emBachelor of Secondary Education (Mathematics):/em Refer to 755102.','N/A','https://www.uow.edu.au/student/finances/domestic-undergraduate/contribution/','https://www.uowcollege.edu.au/courses-pathways/#/'),
('770000','AIM','Bachelor of Music Business','This course will help you master the essentials of the music business. From marketing and artist management to music business economics and law, giving you the skills you need for a lifelong career in the entertainment business.With a balance of theoretical learning with practical, real-world training, you will learn how to collaborate with writers, producers, and performers across our diverse music programs, and build a resilient set of capabilities for the rapidly changing music industry.You will emerge with the leadership, business design, and innovation skills required to successfully manage contemporary organisations in the commercial, public, and not-for-profit sectors.The course can be completed in two years- 6 study periods or part-time equivalent.Delivery Mode: Face to Face with some online components.','Entrepreneur, Booking Agent, Grants Officer, Media Officer, Sales Officer, Artist Manager, Event Manager, Marketing Manager, Label Manager, A&ampR Manager, Venue Manager, Licensing Manager, Promotions Manager, Tour Manager, Business Development Manager, Communications Manager, Sponsorship Manager, Producer, Business Analyst, Policy, Advisor, Promoter.','Business strategy, data and analytics, entertainment law, entrepreneurship, leadership and corporate governance, live performance management, marketing, media and PR, production management.','The course includes a 90-hour internship, where you put your theory into practice. Previous internships include Sony Music, Triple J, APRA/AMCOS, EMI. Collaboration projects with AIM students from other disciplines give you practical experience in music publishing, artist management, partnerships and event management.','https://aim.edu.au/how-to-apply/domestic/fees','https://aim.edu.au/courses/bachelor-of-music-business/'),
('770002','AIM','Bachelor of Music – Composition','This course will train you to become a composer with originality, heightened musical ability, and technical mastery. As digital media expands, so does the demand for talented composers in film, television, video games, and music. This specialisation helps you build a portfolio of work to land paid work and start your career as a composer.You will gain a theoretical and practical understanding of composition for today’s major media and will start building your own portfolio of work from day one. You will collaborate with students from different disciplines including performance and creative technology to create original songs, arrangements, orchestrations, soundtracks, and multimedia installations.The course can be completed in two years - 6 study periods or part-time equivalent. Delivery Mode: Face to Face with some online components.','Arranger/orchestrator, composer, conductor, live performer/instrumentalist, music director, music supervisor, music tutor, recording artist, songwriter, sound designer, ensemble director, ensemble musician, music librarian, music therapist, orchestral musician, private music tutor, professional instrumentalist, music teacher.','Arranging, composition fundamentals, games, installations, music for film, music for new media, music for dance and theatre, music for other media.','Collaboration projects with AIM students from other disciplines give you practical experience in writing, arranging, recording and performing.','https://aim.edu.au/how-to-apply/domestic/fees','https://aim.edu.au/courses/bachelor-of-music-composition/'),
('770004','AIM','Bachelor of Music - Creative Technology','This is more than a traditional audio engineering program. You will go beyond the recording studio combining proven theory with practical experience as you record and create music in unique ways, helping you become a successful audio practitioner and to launch a fulfilling career.You will develop the technical theory and skills required to capture sound, while going beyond the tools themselves. This specialisation places you in a structured, creative environment where you can apply your knowledge in practice.The course can be completed in two years- 6 study periods or part-time equivalent. Delivery Mode: Face to Face with some online components.','Recording &amp mixing, mastering engineer, electronic music programmer, audio-visual technician, broadcast engineer, film and games sound designer, live concert engineer, location sound recordist, music producer, post producer – foley &amp sound effects, ADR, stage sound designer.','Audio delivery, capturing and creating sound, DAWs and mixing consoles, editing sound for other media, post-production, production process, recording techniques, sound system design.','Collaboration projects with AIM students from other disciplines give you practical experience in producing and recording.','https://aim.edu.au/how-to-apply/domestic/fees','https://aim.edu.au/courses/bachelor-of-music-creative-technology/'),
('770006','AIM','Bachelor of Music – Musicology','This course blends research, theory, and philosophy to investigate the cultural history of music in its various forms, and how music is influenced by culture. Discover the practices, values, and ideas to make educated claims about how different people think and feel about the world.You will solidify a foundation in musical literacy, interact with materials that create music, examine how those elements are structured and notated in diverse genres, and develop your skills to identify musical structures by ear.The course can be completed in two years- 6 study periods or part-time equivalent. Delivery Mode: Face to Face with some online components','Ethnomusicology researcher, anthropology researcher, social &amp cultural policy consultant, music critic/reviewer, music editor, music educator, arts administrator, entertainment manager, music journalist, musical director, playlist curator.','Australian music, game music, improvised music, jazz, music and globalisation, music pedagogy, music theatre, popular music, screen music, western art music.','N/A','https://aim.edu.au/how-to-apply/domestic/fees','https://aim.edu.au/courses/bachelor-of-music-musicology/'),
('770008','AIM','Bachelor of Music – Performance','This course will guide you to refine your musicianship, develop your collaboration skills, and help you stand out as a performer. With both a contemporary and classical pathway, you will emerge with the skills and confidence to perform on stage and in the studio.The course can be completed in two years- 6 study periods or part-time equivalent.Delivery Mode: Face to Face with some online components','Live performer/instrumentalist, recording artist, songwriter, ensemble musician, arranger/orchestrator, composer, conductor, music director, music supervisor, music tutor, sound designer, ensemble director, music librarian, music therapist, orchestral musician, private music tutor, professional instrumentalist, music teacher.','You will develop your skills as a performer in your instrument of choice through a mix of one-on-one sessions and group learning. You will participate in collaborative projects with students from other specialisations – including composition and creative technology – to develop your experience working across various areas of music.&nbsp ','Performance practice is developed through both individual tuition and weekly masterclasses, workshops and seminars. Public recitals and collaboration projects develop your skills as a performer. ','https://aim.edu.au/how-to-apply/domestic/fees','https://aim.edu.au/courses/bachelor-of-music-performance/'),
('770010','AIM','Bachelor of Music Theatre','This course is designed for artists seeking to perform at the highest level of music theatre. It prepares you for a professional career on stage, from leading roles to ensemble work and the creation of original productions.Through rigorous, practice-led training, you will develop advanced capabilities in singing, dance and acting, supported by personalised one-on-one tuition and guidance from experienced industry professionals.You will refine your technique, elevate your stagecraft, and cultivate the presence and discipline required of a professional performer. Alongside this, you will build a sustainable performance practice, grounded in a deep understanding of the psychology of performance.Graduating with substantial performance experience and a distinct artistic identity, you will be equipped to enter the industry as a versatile, confident and highly skilled music theatre artist.This course can be completed in 9 Study Periods (3 years) full-time.Delivery Mode: Face to Face with some online components.','Music theatre performer, actor, dancer, casting agent, composer for music theatre, music theatre director, voice over specialist, music journalist, performing arts teacher, stage manager, vocalist/singer. ','Acting, dance, performance, the singing actor, voice.','Students have the opportunity to participate in the annual musical production. ','https://aim.edu.au/how-to-apply/domestic/fees','https://aim.edu.au/courses/bachelor-of-music-theatre/'),
('770012','AIM','Diploma of Music Business','In this course you will learn the principles of effective management, in this ever-changing industry, and discover where you might fit in the diverse arts and entertainment business.At the end of this course, you may continue to complete the a href=\" Bachelor of Music Business\" \"noopener noreferrer\" \"_blank\" Bachelor of Music Business which will further develop your skills and knowledge and provide the opportunity for an industry internship.','Entrepreneur, booking assistant, grants assistant, media coordinator, sales rep, event coordinator, marketing assistant, label assistant, A&ampR assistant, venue assistant, licensing officer, promotions assistant, communications coordinator, studio assistant, promoter.','Entertainment law, Leadership and Corporate Governance, Marketing, Media and PR.','N/A','https://aim.edu.au/how-to-apply/domestic/fees','https://aim.edu.au/courses/bachelor-of-music-composition/'),
('770014','AIM','Diploma of Music','This course is an ideal starting point for a career in music, helping you to build your musical literacy and academic skills in just 12 months. Walk away with an industry-recognised qualification, or transition to a Bachelor program – the choice is yours.','Performer, songwriter, session musician, producer, mixing engineer assistant, FOH engineering assistant, solo artist, A&ampR assistant, record label assistant.','Specialise in composition, creative technology or performance.','N/A','https://aim.edu.au/how-to-apply/domestic/fees','https://aim.edu.au/courses/diploma-of-music/'),
('770020','AIM','Bachelor of Music (Music Business)','span \": white color: black\"The Bachelor of Music (Music Business) program combines music practice with business, giving you incredible skills to navigate the modern music landscape. span \": white color: black\"Grow your career as a self-managed independent artist or run a business in the music industry. The course can be completed in 6 study periods (2 years full-time) or part-time equivalent.Delivery Mode: Face to Face with some online components.','Artist Manager, A&ampR Manager, Music Publisher, Concert, Tour &amp Festival Promoter, Entertainment Publicist, Event Manager, Recording Artist, Marketing &amp Sales, Performer, Producer, Venue Manager.','Artist entrepreneurship, career development and long-term success strategies, creative artistry and performance development, music business and industry practices.','N/A','https://aim.edu.au/how-to-apply/domestic/fees','https://aim.edu.au/courses/bachelor-of-music-music-business/'),
('770030','AIM','Undergraduate Certificate in Music','The Undergraduate Certificate in Music is a 100% online course for anyone interested in deepening their skill and knowledge around music. With no assumed knowledge of music theory, you can choose a study path focused on your interests, from performance and composing, to producers and audio engineers.','span \"(0, 0, 0) background-\"Composer, live performer, music arranger, music conductor, music producer, music theatre performer, musical performer – recording/live, performing arts teacher, private music tutor, sound designer, studio recording engineer, videogame composer.','Audio, composition, creative technology, music production, performance.','span \"background- (0, 0, 0)\"Through the study of four specialisation modules (2 per study period), students will focus on developing the creative, technical, and professional skills required by professional music practitioners, and explore the roles, skills and resources required to convert creative ideas into marketable commodities. It will enable students to build musical flexibility through the development of musical literacy and collaborative techniques. Studying the Undergraduate Certificate in Music encourages the development of digital technology skills and online music making.','https://aim.edu.au/how-to-apply/domestic/fees','https://aim.edu.au/courses/undergraduate-cert-music-online/'),
('771000','SPJGM','Bachelor of Data Science','In today’s rapidly digitising world, data science has emerged as a game changer, driving groundbreaking decisions and innovations across industries. From uncovering emerging trends to solving complex challenges, data analytics is fundamentally transforming how organisations operate and strategise. As sectors from healthcare to finance increasingly rely on data-driven decision-making, the demand for skilled data scientists has grown dramatically. \nSP Jain Global’s Bachelor of Data Science is a rigorous three-year full-time program designed to prepare students for success in this dynamic field. The curriculum balances theoretical knowledge with practical application, ensuring graduates are well-equipped for the data-driven landscape. It provides:\n \n balanced focus on mathematical foundations and industry applications \n 70-80% of the curriculum dedicated to skill development and practical application \n covers a wide range of subjects including Advanced Analytics, Machine Learning, Big Data Processing, and Statistical Data Analysis \n','Graduates are prepared for roles in various industries including IT, consulting, BFSI, healthcare, education, retail, and media. potential positions include data scientists, data analysts, data developers and data consultants.','Advanced analytics (stream, sensor and spatio-temporal analysis), advanced calculus, advanced linear algebra and applications, algorithms and data structures, Big Data processing techniques and platforms, communication, consumer behaviour and marketing research, data integration and warehousing, data mining, computer programming, databases, emotional intelligence, innovation, creativity and agility, leadership, machine learning, mathematics for data scientists, object relational and NoSQL databases, programming for analytics, simulation modelling, social web analytics (web, Internet of Things, and social media mining), statistics and probability, statistical data analysis, teamwork and global dexterity, visual analytics/explorative data analysis.','Real-world projects in collaboration with industry leaders.Skill-building workshops on topics such as SAS JMP, AWS and Azure Cloud, DevOps, and MLOps.Opportunities for industry certifications.Multiple internship opportunities throughout the program (past internship partners: Amazon, KPMG, Uber, Macquarie Group, UPilot, Wolters Kluwer, Instagram, Adaptive Investments and more).','https://www.spjain.edu.au/','https://www.spjain.edu.au/programs/undergraduate/bachelor-of-data-science'),
('771001','SPJGM','Undergraduate Certificate of Data Science','Every day, data scientists are shaping the world as we know it. The a href=\"http://www3.weforum.org/docs/WEF_Future_of_Jobs_2020.pdf\" \"_blank\"World Economic Forum’s Future of Jobs Report 2020 predicts that by 2025, the role with the highest growth in demand will be that of Data Analysts and Scientists. Take the first step towards making your career future-ready with the Undergraduate Certificate of Data Science (UCDS) offered by SP Jain School of Global Management.','Junior data analyst, junior SQL developer, junior business analyst and data analyst intern.','Data science, data solutions, mathematics, programming, python.','N/A','https://www.spjain.edu.au/','https://www.spjain.edu.au/lp/undergraduate-certificate-of-data-science'),
('772000','UNSWC','Diploma of Architecture','span \"(0, 0, 0)\"The UNSW College Diploma of Architecture is your direct pathway to second year at UNSW Sydney - one of the world&#39s top 20 universities.*span \"(0, 0, 0)\"Designed for students who narrowly missed direct entry, this 12-month program offers a supportive and practical introduction to university life with smaller classes, personalised academic support, and first-year equivalent courses developed in collaboration with UNSW Sydney.span \"(0, 0, 0)\"You&#39ll gain the design thinking, technical skills, and creative confidence to thrive in a range of architecture disciplines, while building your portfolio through studio-based learning. You&#39ll explore how people, place and purpose intersect in the built environment, and gain hands-on experience with digital tools and industry-relevant approaches.span \"(0, 0, 0)\"Whether you&#39re interested in architectural studies, interior architecture or landscape architecture, this Diploma gives you the foundation you need and a direct path to your UNSW degree.span \"(0, 0, 0)\"Upon successful completion of the Diploma and meeting entry requirements, you&#39ll progress into second year at UNSW Sydney where you can study:span \"(0, 0, 0)\"Bachelor of Architectural Studiesspan \"(0, 0, 0)\"Bachelor of Interior Architecture (Honours) orspan \"(0, 0, 0)\"Bachelor of Landscape Architecture (Honours)span \"(0, 0, 0)\"* QS World University Rankings, 2026.','span \"(0, 0, 0)\"Landscape architect, architect, architectural technician, interior and spatial designer, building surveyor, town planner, production designer.','span \"(0, 0, 0)\"Architectural studies, interior architecture, landscape architecture.','N/A','https://www.unswcollege.edu.au/apply/fees?studentType=domestic','https://www.unswcollege.edu.au/study/domestic-diplomas/diploma-of-architecture'),
('772001','UNSWC','Diploma of Business','span \"(0, 0, 0)\"Start your career in business with the UNSW College Diploma of Business, a 12-month program that leads you straight into second year of the Bachelor of Commerce at UNSW Sydney.span \"(0, 0, 0)\"Designed for students who narrowly missed direct entry, the Diploma delivers a full first-year university experience in a supportive learning environment. You&#39ll benefit from smaller class sizes, personalised academic support, and first-year equivalent courses developed in close collaboration with UNSW Business School. The program equips you with the foundational knowledge and skills to succeed in areas like marketing, management, finance, and more.span \"(0, 0, 0)\"Upon successful completion of the Diploma and meeting the required progression criteria, you&#39ll enter second year of the UNSW Bachelor of Commerce, one of Australia&#39s most sought-after business degrees.span \"(0, 0, 0)\"UNSW Sydney is ranked among the world’s top 20 universities* and is home to Australia’s most employable graduates^. At UNSW, you’ll learn from world-class academics, connect with industry leaders, and choose from a wide range of specialisations to shape your future in business.span \"(0, 0, 0)\"* QS World University Rankings, 2026.span \"(0, 0, 0)\"^ Most employable graduates for six years in a row - AFR Top 100 Future Leaders Awards, 2020–2025.','span \"(0, 0, 0)\"Accountant, brand manager, business analyst, entrepreneur, financial adviser, fintech project manager, HR consultant, investment banker, management consultant, social media manager, start-up founder, strategist.','span \"(0, 0, 0)\"Accounting, behavioural economics, business analytics, business economics, span \"(41, 42, 46) background-\"business sustainability and social impact, span \"(0, 0, 0)\"cybersecurity management, finance, financial technology, human resource management, information systems, span \"(41, 42, 46) background-\"innovation, strategy and entrepreneurshipspan \"(0, 0, 0)\", international business, marketing, marketing analytics, taxation.','N/A','https://www.unswcollege.edu.au/apply/fees?studentType=domestic','https://www.unswcollege.edu.au/study/domestic-diplomas/diploma-of-business'),
('772002','UNSWC','Diploma of Computer Science','span \"(0, 0, 0)\"Start your journey in tech with the UNSW College Diploma of Computer Science, a 12-month program that leads you straight into second year of the Bachelor of Science (Computer Science) at UNSW Sydney.span \"(0, 0, 0)\"Designed for students who narrowly missed direct entry to UNSW, the Diploma offers a full first-year university experience in a supportive environment. You&#39ll benefit from smaller class sizes, personalised academic support, and first-year equivalent courses developed in collaboration with UNSW&#39s leading Computer Science faculty.span \"(0, 0, 0)\"In this Diploma, you&#39ll learn about the design, construction and uses of computer systems with an emphasis on the basic principles behind computing tools, operating systems, compilers and translators, and computer hardware.span \"(0, 0, 0)\"Upon successful completion of the Diploma and meeting the required progression criteria, you&#39ll be ready to take your place in the second year of the Bachelor of Science (Computer Science) at UNSW Sydney.span \"(0, 0, 0)\"UNSW Sydney is ranked #1 in Australia and #25th globally for Engineering and Technology* and is home to Australia’s most employable graduates^, six years in a row. With cutting-edge facilities, leading researchers, and a thriving tech community, you’ll be ready to shape the future of computing and innovation.span \"(0, 0, 0)\"* QS World University Rankings by Subject, 2025.span \"(0, 0, 0)\"^ Most employable graduates for six years in a row – AFR Top 100 Future Leaders Awards, 2020–2025.','span \"(0, 0, 0)\"Cyber security consultant, information systems manager, database administrator, systems analyst, IT consultant, software developer, systems engineer, game programmer.','span \"(0, 0, 0)\"Artificial intelligence, computer networks, computer science, database systems, ecommerce systems, embedded systems, programming languages, security engineering.','N/A','https://www.unswcollege.edu.au/apply/fees?studentType=domestic','https://www.unswcollege.edu.au/study/domestic-diplomas/diploma-of-computer-science'),
('772003','UNSWC','Diploma of Engineering','span \"(0, 0, 0)\"A UNSW College Diploma of Engineering is more than just a qualification – it’s your pathway to UNSW Sydney, Australia’s most employable university*, and the #1 Engineering faculty in the country.^span \"(0, 0, 0)\"In just 12 months, this supportive program prepares you to transition seamlessly into the second year of a UNSW Engineering degree.span \"(0, 0, 0)\"Designed for students who have missed the entry requirements, the Diploma of Engineering offers smaller classes, personalised support, and additional learning time to help you excel in fields like civil, mechanical, electrical, and environmental engineering.span \"(0, 0, 0)\"Upon successful completion of the Diploma and meeting the required progression criteria, you’ll be ready to take your place in the second year of the Bachelor of Engineering (Honours) at UNSW Sydney, where you can choose your major. Work with robots, boost energy production or design bionic limbs – it’s all possible at UNSW Sydney. span \"(0, 0, 0)\"UNSW are world leaders in engineering education and research. As a UNSW student, you’ll join a vibrant and connected community, with opportunities to expand your network socially and professionally through clubs, societies, and industry events.span \"(0, 0, 0)\"* Most employable graduates for six years in a row - AFR Top 100 Future Leaders Awards, 2020–2025.span \"(0, 0, 0)\"^ QS World University Rankings by subject, 2025.','span \"(0, 0, 0)\"Aerospace engineer, Bioinformatics engineer, Civil engineer, Chemical engineer, Computer engineer, Electrical engineer, Mechanical engineer, Mining engineer, Telecommunications engineer.','span \"background- (41, 42, 46)\"Aerospace engineering, bioinformatics, biomedical engineering, chemical engineering, chemical product engineering, civil engineering, computer engineering, electrical engineering, environmental engineering, geoenergy and geostorage, mechanical &amp manufacturing engineering, mechanical engineering, mining engineering, nuclear engineering, photovoltaics &amp solar energy engineering, quantum engineering, renewable energy engineering, robotics &amp mechatronics engineering, surveying, software engineering, telecommunications.','N/A','https://www.unswcollege.edu.au/apply/fees?studentType=domestic','https://www.unswcollege.edu.au/study/domestic-diplomas/diploma-of-engineering'),
('772004','UNSWC','Diploma of Media and Communications','span \"(0, 0, 0)\"A UNSW College Diploma of Media and Communications is your pathway to a Bachelor of Media at UNSW Sydney, home to Australia’s most employable graduates*.span \"(0, 0, 0)\"Designed for students who narrowly missed direct entry to UNSW, the 12-month Diploma offers a complete first-year university experience in a creative and supportive environment. With smaller class sizes, personalised academic support, and first-year equivalent courses developed in collaboration with UNSW Sydney, you’ll gain practical skills and confidence in areas like storytelling, screen production, public relations, and digital content creation.span \"(0, 0, 0)\"Upon successful completion of the Diploma and meeting the required progression criteria, you’ll progress into second year of the Bachelor of Media at UNSW Sydney, where you’ll explore how media shapes society and drives cultural and social change.span \"(0, 0, 0)\"UNSW Sydney is home to world-leading academics and industry-connected experts who will help you develop critical thinking, creative strategy, and hands-on production capabilities. Ranked #1 in Australia and 32nd globally^ for employment outcomes. UNSW equips you with the skills to make an impact across journalism, communications, and digital media in a fast-evolving global landscape and become one of Australia’s most employable graduates.*span \"(0, 0, 0)\"^ QS World University Rankings, 2026.span \"(0, 0, 0)\"* Most employable graduates for six years in a row – AFR Top 100 Future Leaders Awards, 2020–2025.','span \"(0, 0, 0)\"Corporate communications manager, advertising strategist, public relations consultant, brand manager, journalist, filmmaker, animator, copywriter, publicist, media advisor.','span \"(0, 0, 0)\"Cinema studies, communication and journalism, media studies, public relations and advertising, screen production.','N/A','https://www.unswcollege.edu.au/apply/fees?studentType=domestic','https://www.unswcollege.edu.au/study/domestic-diplomas/diploma-of-media-communications'),
('772005','UNSWC','Diploma of Science','span \"(0, 0, 0)\"Start your science journey with the UNSW College Diploma of Science, a 12-month program that leads you straight into second year of the Bachelor of Science at UNSW Sydney.span \"(0, 0, 0)\"Designed for students who narrowly missed direct university entry, the Diploma offers a full first-year experience in a supportive academic environment. With smaller class sizes, personalised support, and first-year equivalent courses developed in collaboration with UNSW Science, you’ll gain the foundational knowledge and practical skills to succeed in fields like biotechnology, environmental science, physics, neuroscience, and more.span \"(0, 0, 0)\"Upon successful completion of the Diploma and meeting the required progression criteria, you’ll enter second year of the UNSW Bachelor of Science, a degree known for its flexibility, real-world focus, and research excellence.span \"(0, 0, 0)\"At UNSW Sydney, you’ll learn from world-class academics and access cutting-edge labs and facilities. With opportunities to explore diverse disciplines, engage with industry, and join a vibrant student community, you’ll graduate ready to lead, innovate, and make an impact — at the home of Australia’s most employable graduates*. UNSW Sydney is ranked #1 in Australia and 32nd globally^ for employment outcomes.span \"(0, 0, 0)\"* Most employable graduates for six years in a row - AFR Top 100 Future Leaders Awards, 2020–2025.span \"(0, 0, 0)\"^ QS World University Rankings, 2026.','span \"(0, 0, 0)\"Environmental scientist, epidemiologist, geophysicist, hospital technician, marine biologist, medical doctor, medical lab scientist, nutritionist, pharmacist, science educator, scientist, veterinary scientist.','span \"(0, 0, 0)\"Anatomy, span \"(41, 42, 46) background-\"biology and biodiversityspan \"(0, 0, 0)\", chemistry, food science, genetics, marine and coastal science, materials science, mathematics, microbiology, molecular and cell biology, pathology, pharmacology, physical oceanography, physics, physiology, statistics.','N/A','https://www.unswcollege.edu.au/apply/fees?studentType=domestic','https://www.unswcollege.edu.au/study/domestic-diplomas/diploma-of-science'),
('773000','JMC','Bachelor of Music with major in Contemporary Performance','The world just can’t get enough of the magic of the moving image, and the global uptake of digital technology is creating unprecedented demand for professional content creators.From producers to directors, cinematographers, scriptwriters, motion graphics designers, editors and more, entertainment production is big business. Film and TV at JMC Academy is a hands-on production-based course that will give you the knowledge and the creative, technical and managerial skills to create and produce leading content for film, TV, live broadcasts, documentaries, commercials and music videos.Develop your creative expression and technical skills whilst mastering screenwriting, directing, cinematography, motion graphics and post-production, to launch your creative career.We take film and TV seriously at JMC, with studios full of the best tech in the trade. You’ll have access to highly sophisticated equipment and recording studios, including RED EPIC-W™ HELIUM™ 8K, Arri Amira series and Blackmagic Design Ursa Broadcast G2 cameras, green-screen studios, editing suites, colour grading equipment including powerful iMac Pros and Blackmagic Design DaVinci Resolve, a cinema/theatre fitted with 5.1 surround sound and full student loan facilities with lenses, cameras, lights and sound equipment available.With world class campuses in Sydney, Melbourne, and Brisbane, a dedicated team of academics and industry professional lecturers, and the opportunity to participate in international masterclasses and study abroad programs, JMC Academy is committed to ensuring our graduates make their own indelible mark on industry.All JMC, bachelor degree graduates are eligible to apply for entry into JMC Academy&#39s Master of Creative Industries, or relevant post-grad qualifications at any Australian university.','Director, cinematographer, scriptwriter, editor, producer, production manager, post-production supervisor, technical director, motion graphics designer, lighting designer, sound recordist, camera operator.','Broadcasting, camera operation, camera and lighting, cinematography, directing (film), directing (television), documentary production, film audio, film composition, film editing, filmmaking, industry and professional development, international cinema, lighting design, span \"background- (31, 31, 31)\"mise en scène, motion graphics, multi-cam broadcasting, music videos, popular culture, postproduction, producing (film), producing (television), screen history, screen and genre studies, screenwriting, short films, sound design, sound recording and design, television broadcasting, television studio production.','At JMC we have a dedicated Internship Program as well as work placement opportunities designed to have students apply their learning and gain hands-on experience in real industry roles.','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/study-at-jmc/domestic-fees-financial-aid/','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/our-courses/film-television-production/bachelor-of-creative-arts-film-television/'),
('773001','JMC','Diploma of Music with major in Contemporary Performance','Designed for aspiring performers ready to make an impact, the Diploma of Music (Contemporary Performance) offers a fast-tracked, practical introduction to the music industry. In just 8 months of full-time study, you’ll sharpen your technical skills, explore your artistic identity, and gain real-world performance experience across a range of contemporary genres.\nFrom day one, you’ll rehearse and perform in industry-standard spaces equipped with top-tier gear—developing the confidence and stagecraft needed for a professional career. You’ll also collaborate with peers across songwriting, production and business, building a network that mirrors the realities of today’s music scene.\nWhether you’re planning to launch your music career or pathway into the Bachelor of Music, this course provides a strong foundation for both.','Emerging recording artist, live performer, session musician, band member, artist manager (self-managed), music tutor, event support roles, or continue into further study such as the Bachelor of Music.','Core musicianship, ear training, ensemble performance, instrumental technique (guitar, bass, drums, keys, voice), introduction to songwriting, and use of industry-standard music software and production tools, music business fundamentals, music theory, stagecraft.','Throughout the course, students gain hands-on performance experience at JMC’s on-campus venues and curated live events. You’ll also have the opportunity to collaborate with peers across JMC’s creative disciplines, reflecting real-world industry collaboration.','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/study-at-jmc/domestic-fees-financial-aid/','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/our-courses/contemporary-music-performance/diploma-of-music-with-major-in-contemporary-performance/'),
('773002','JMC','Bachelor of Music with major in Songwriting','There are few things more exciting than writing your own music and bringing it to life. JMC Academy’s Songwriting course is renowned for its hands-on practicality, a strong focus on individual musicianship, connections to national songwriting body APRA AMCOS and renowned international music exchange programs. This course provides a strong launchpad into the entertainment industry for all up-and-coming songwriters and composers. \nCovering the essential tools for writing music to appeal to publishers, record labels and producers across a variety of genres and media channels, this course will help you to create your own music and lyrics, develop your instrumental skills, produce demos and perform your own songs. \nThis course is designed to help you create strong, focused songs that perfectly blend your lyrical ideas with powerful melodies. Songwriting at JMC is one of the 3 majors offered under the Bachelor of Music. Other major areas include: \n \n contemporary performance \n songwriting  \n music production.  \n\nJMC’s firm commitment to providing you with the best technology in the trade can be seen in our fully fitted songwriting suites, designed for recording in high quality and for mastering production techniques. Each songwriting suite features software like ProTools, Logic Pro X, Ableton Live, and Native Instruments, along with MIDI keyboard controllers (keyboard and pad), high-quality monitors, and an array of Rode Condenser mics and instrument microphones. \nWith world class campuses in Sydney, Melbourne and Brisbane, a dedicated team of academics and industry professional lecturers, and the opportunity to participate in international masterclasses, music and songwriting camps and study abroad programs, JMC Academy is committed to ensuring our graduates make their own indelible mark on industry. \nExtend your studies with our new double degree! JMC Academy’s Bachelor of Music and Bachelor of Entertainment Business Management offers you a new way to pair technical and creative skills in music with the essential business know-how required to understand all facets of the music business industry. This unique blend of artistry and business acumen equips students with the skills to successfully manage their own career and transform their music into a marketable product. \nAll JMC bachelor degree graduates are eligible to apply for entry into JMC Academy’s Master of Creative Industries, or relevant post-grad qualification at any Australian university. ','Performing singer/songwriter, lyricist, freelance songwriter, composer, published songwriter, advertising creative(jingle writer for TV/radio), professional arranger, music producer, music publisher, music teacher.','Arranging, arranging for band and orchestra, bass guitar, contemporary music performance, directed studies, directed studies in songwriting, drums, ear training, electronic music, ensemble studies, guitar, instrument studies, lyric writing, lyric and songwriting, lyrics and literature, music business, music cultures, music history, music production, music technology, music theory, piano/keyboards, screen music, song writing, songwriting and composition, special projects, tutoring techniques, voice. ','At JMC we have a dedicated Internship Program as well as work placement opportunities designed to have students apply their learning and gain hands-on experience in real industry projects. ','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/study-at-jmc/domestic-fees-financial-aid/','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/'),
('773003','JMC','Diploma of Music with major in Songwriting','There are few things more exciting than writing your own music and bringing it to life. The Diploma of Music with major in Songwriting at JMC Academy is a practical, 8-month course designed to help emerging songwriters turn their musical ideas into powerful, original works.\nWith a strong focus on individual musicianship, collaboration, and creative development, this course equips you with the essential skills to write, perform, and record songs that resonate. You’ll learn to craft lyrics and melodies that connect, while also gaining experience in performance, music production, and industry fundamentals.\nConnected with national body APRA AMCOS and international songwriting networks, JMC offers a dynamic foundation for launching your songwriting career or for continuing into the Bachelor of Music.','Junior songwriter, performing singer/songwriter, demo artist, content creator, freelance lyricist, or a pathway into the Bachelor of Music for further specialisation.','Arranging, arranging for band and orchestra, bass guitar, contemporary music performance, directed studies, directed studies in songwriting, drums, ear training, electronic music, ensemble studies, guitar, instrument studies, lyric writing, lyric and songwriting, lyrics and literature, music business, music cultures, music history, music production, music technology, music theory, piano/keyboards, screen music, song writing, songwriting and composition, special projects, tutoring techniques, voice.','Students workshop and perform original songs from the outset, receiving feedback from industry professionals and collaborating across JMC’s creative disciplines in real-world project settings.','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/study-at-jmc/domestic-fees-financial-aid/','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/our-courses/songwriting/diploma-of-music-with-major-in-songwriting/'),
('773004','JMC','Bachelor of Creative Technology (Audio Engineering and Sound production)','Do you get inspired by the little sounds no-one else stops to hear? Start studying within a world class studio environment from day one, collaborate with your peers, intern on real industry practical projects, build your portfolio and be mentored by connected industry professionals through Australia&#39s leading Audio Engineering course.Audio Engineering and Sound Production is a hands-on production-based course that is directly in sync with the audio industry.In line with our commitment to helping you curate your sound, your course and your future, after studying a base of core audio and sound fundamentals in trimester 1, you will then have the choice to specialise in one of four elective streams live events, electronic music production, sound and media or studio recording and mixing enabling you to engage with the content and path that best suits and interests you.We take Audio seriously at JMC, with our Sydney campus boasting some of the best recording studios in the Southern Hemisphere. Our studios are full of the best tech in the trade including high-end equipment and recording studios fitted with 5.1 surround sound and all the latest gear, including: Consoles: SSL Duality 48 Channel, Avid C24 control surface, Pro Tools HD with Avid HDX conversion Mics: Neumann U87, FET 47, U89, Royer 121, AKG C414 and many more Plugins: Full Universal Audio Plugin Suite, Waves Mercury Bundle Outboard: Avalon 2022, Universal Audio 2x610, Empirical Labs Distressors.With advanced design campuses in Sydney, Melbourne and Brisbane, a dedicated team of academics and industry professional lecturers, and the opportunity to participate in international masterclasses and study abroad programs, JMC Academy is committed to ensuring our graduates make their own indelible mark on industry.Extend your studies with our new double degree. JMC Academy&#39s Bachelor of Creative Technology (Audio Engineering and Sound Production) and Bachelor of Entertainment Business Management offers you a new way to pair technical skills in audio and sound with the essential business know-how required to succeed in the ever-evolving entertainment industry. This unique blend of artistry and business acumen allows audio engineers to seamlessly navigate both the audio and the music business world, gaining the expertise to manage their own business or freelance career.All JMC, bachelor degree graduates are eligible to apply for entry into JMC Academy&#39s Master of Creative Industries, or relevant post-grad qualifications at any Australian university.','Music producer, mix engineer, production coordinator, recording engineer, studio manager/owner, AV specialist, location sound engineer, sound designer, stage technician, live sound engineer, postproduction engineer, acoustician/environmental acoustics.','Acoustic design, acoustics theory, audio, audio and sound theory, audio engineering, audio industry, audio post production, audio system design, electronic music, electronics, foley, history of Western recording, live sound, music business, music history, music production, music production analysis, musical instrument digital interface (MIDI), recording, research project, sound art, sound design, sound recording, spacial recording, studio recording, TV, radio and film audio.','Throughout the course, students gain hands-on performance experience at JMC’s on-campus venues and curated live events. You’ll also have the opportunity to collaborate with peers across JMC’s creative disciplines, reflecting real-world industry collaboration.','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/study-at-jmc/domestic-fees-financial-aid/','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/our-courses/audio-engineering-sound-production/bachelor-of-creative-technology-audio-engineering-and-sound-production/'),
('773005','JMC','Diploma of Audio Engineering and Sound Production','Do you get inspired by the little sounds no-one else stops to hear? Start studying within a world class studio environment from day one, collaborate with your peers, intern on real industry practical projects, build your portfolio and be mentored by connected industry professionals through Australia&#39s leading Audio Engineering course.Audio Engineering and Sound Production is a hands-on production-based course that is directly in sync with the audio industry.In line with our commitment to helping you curate your sound, your course and your future, after studying a base of core audio and sound fundamentals in trimester 1, you will then have the choice to specialise in one of four elective streams live events, electronic music production, sound and media or studio recording and mixing enabling you to engage with the content and path that best suits and interests you.We take Audio seriously at JMC, with our Sydney campus boasting some of the best recording studios in the Southern Hemisphere. Our studios are full of the best tech in the trade including high-end equipment and recording studios fitted with 5.1 surround sound and all the latest gear, including: Consoles: SSL Duality 48 Channel, Avid C24 control surface, Pro Tools HD with Avid HDX conversion Mics: Neumann U87, FET 47, U89, Royer 121, AKG C414 and many more Plugins: Full Universal Audio Plugin Suite, Waves Mercury Bundle Outboard: Avalon 2022, Universal Audio 2x610, Empirical Labs Distressors.With advanced design campuses in Sydney, Melbourne and Brisbane, a dedicated team of academics and industry professional lecturers, and the opportunity to participate in international masterclasses and study abroad programs, JMC Academy is committed to ensuring our graduates make their own indelible mark on industry.Extend your studies with our new double degree! JMC Academy&#39s Bachelor of Creative Technology (Audio Engineering and Sound Production) and Bachelor of Entertainment Business Management offers you a new way to pair technical skills in audio and sound with the essential business know-how required to succeed in the ever-evolving entertainment industry. This unique blend of artistry and business acumen allows audio engineers toseamlessly navigate both the audio and the music business world, gaining the expertise to manage their own business or freelance career.All JMC, bachelor degree graduates are eligible to apply for entry into JMC Academy&#39s Master of Creative Industries, or relevant post-grad qualifications at any Australian university.','Music producer, mix engineer, production coordinator, recording engineer, studio manager/owner, AV specialist, location sound engineer, sound designer, stage technician, live sound engineer, postproduction engineer, acoustician/environmental acoustics. ','Acoustic design, acoustics theory, audio, audio and sound theory, audio engineering, audio industry, audio post production, audio system design, electronic music, electronics, foley, history of Western recording, live sound, music business, music history, music production, music production analysis, musical instrument digital interface (MIDI), recording, research project, sound art, sound design, sound recording, spacial recording, studio recording, TV, radio and film audio. ','At JMC we have a dedicated Internship Program as well as work placement opportunities designed to have students apply their learning and gain hands-on experience in real industry roles. ','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/study-at-jmc/domestic-fees-financial-aid/','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/our-courses/audio-engineering-sound-production/diploma-of-audio-engineering-sound-production/'),
('773006','JMC','Bachelor of Entertainment Business Management','Entertainment Business Management at JMC is rewarding, innovative and inspiring. Offering you the best of both worlds, this course is designed to teach you cutting-edge business and management skills along with the contextual knowledge and practice applicable to the exciting and expansive world of entertainment.\nBe taught and mentored directly by those who have carved out their own successful careers in the areas of artist and event management, music publishing, label management, and marketing whilst gaining a deep understanding of the industry and how to succeed in it. \nYou will develop specific skills in artist management, event and festival management, marketing, entrepreneurship, business planning, contract negotiations, budgeting and finance, copyright and intellectual property. All while a href=\"https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/about-us/our-partners/\" \"_blank\"building your own enviable network of industry and peer contacts along the way.\nWith world class campuses in Sydney, Melbourne and Brisbane, a dedicated team of academics and industry professional lecturers, and the opportunity to participate in international masterclasses and study abroad programs, JMC Academy is committed to ensuring our graduates make their own indelible mark on industry. \nAll JMC bachelor degree graduates are eligible to apply for entry into JMC Academy’s Master of Creative Industries, or relevant post-grad qualification at any Australian university. ','Artist manager, talent manager, booking agent, promoter, event manager, stage manager, digital marketer, licensing agent, promotions director, label manager, A&ampR manager, sales director, media director, copyright/royalties manager, licensing manager, music production manager, promotions manager, media publisher, festival organiser, radio content producer, social media strategist, music co-ordinator.','Accounting, branding, business, copyright and publishing, deal making, digital content creation, entertainment history, entertainment management, entertainment marketing, entrepreneurialism, event management, events, festival management, film and television production management, finance, funding, international licensing and branding, licensing, management theory, marketing, online management systems, production management, professional communication, professional practice, professional projects, promotions, publicity, stage management, talent development (A+R), tour management. ','At JMC we have a dedicated Internship Program as well as work placement opportunities designed to have students apply their learning and gain hands-on experience in real industry roles. The placements for this course are numerous and include labels, established music festivals, large-scale events and more. ','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/study-at-jmc/domestic-fees-financial-aid/','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/'),
('773007','JMC','Diploma of Entertainment Business Management','Do you dream of finding the next big artist, producing the ultimate gig or managing TV and film sets? JMC Academy’s Diploma of Entertainment Business Management gives you the fundamental understanding of entertainment business to help you succeed as a creative industries manager.This Diploma will provide you with a core understanding of entertainment business practices in talent development, marketing, copyright and publishing. Then, you will put your learnings into practice, gaining skills and hands-on experience in stage and production management to help bring entertainment events to life.','Artist manager, talent manager, booking agent, promoter, event manager, stage manager, digital marketer, licensing agent, promotions director, label manager, A and R manager, sales director, media director, copyright/royalties manager, licensing manager, music production manager, promotions manager, media publisher, festival organiser, radio content producer, social media strategist, music co-ordinator. ','Accounting, branding, business, copyright + publishing, deal making, digital content creation, entertainment history, entertainment management, entertainment marketing, entrepreneurialism, event management, events, festival management, film + television production management, finance, funding, international licencing and branding, licencing, management theory, marketing, online management systems, production management, professional communication, professional practice, professional projects, promotions, publicity, stage management, talent development (A+R), tour management.','At JMC we have a dedicated Internship Program as well as work placement opportunities designed to have students apply their learning and gain hands-on experience in real industry roles. The placements for this course are numerous and include labels, established music festivals, large-scale events and more.','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/study-at-jmc/domestic-fees-financial-aid/','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/our-courses/entertainment-business-management/diploma-of-entertainment-business-management/'),
('773008','JMC','Bachelor of Creative Arts (Animation)','Animation at JMC involves more than just bringing a character to life through technical ability. Through association with studio professionals from Pixar and Animal Logic, JMC Animation is born of a love affair between technology, creativity and science.Animation is an essential ingredient in the collaborative, innovative and future-forward global entertainment industry, which is why some of the most in-demand players are animators and visual-effects specialists. Learn to design and develop characters and worlds – from concept to finished art – and create believable character performances and arresting graphical motion.Take advantage of JMC’s industry-standard technology to bring your project to life, and add to your skills, with extension electives like augmented and virtual reality, motion capture, and compositing.Build a polished portfolio and showreel and learn the essential skills of working in a studio with professional colleagues. You will be able to access the Full Adobe Creative Cloud Suite, Autodesk Maya, Wacom Intuos Pro + Cintiq tablets, Animation lightboxes, ball + socket stop-motion rigs, Dragonframe stop-motion software, Rokoko Motion Capture System, VR facilities, green-screen studios, renderers (Redshift, Pixar RenderMan, Arnold), Substance Painter for texturing, Zbrush for sculpting, Compositing tools (After Effects, Nuke), Katana for Look Development and Shotgun Studio for Project Planning + Management.With world class campuses in Sydney, Melbourne, and Brisbane, a dedicated team of academics and industry professional lecturers, and the opportunity to participate in international masterclasses and study abroad programs, JMC Academy is committed to ensuring our graduates make their own indelible mark on industry.All JMC bachelor degree graduates are eligible to apply for entry into JMC Academy&#39s Master of Creative Industries, or relevant post-grad qualification at any Australian university.','Animator, director, producer, storyboard artist, character designer, art director, modeler, motion graphic designer, production coordinator, concept artist, compositor.','3D animation, 3D modelling, character design, compositing, concept art, concept development, creative process, digital art, digital sculpture, motion capture, motion design, production art, professional + industry development, rendering, screen literacy, studio skills, traditional animation (2D), visual narrative, visual storytelling. ','At JMC we have a dedicated Internship Program as well as work placement opportunities designed to have students apply their learning and gain hands-on experience in real industry roles. ','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/study-at-jmc/domestic-fees-financial-aid/','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/our-courses/animation/bachelor-of-creative-arts-animation/'),
('773009','JMC','Diploma of Creative Arts (Animation)','Animation at JMC Academy is underpinned by a strong understanding of design, storytelling and image-making. The Diploma of Creative Arts (Animation) is an intensive 8-month course that offers a hands-on introduction to animation for film, games and visual communication.\nYou’ll explore the process of bringing characters and worlds to life, from initial sketches to fully rendered digital sequences. Along the way, you’ll gain foundational skills in drawing, 2D and 3D animation, visual storytelling and motion design. Taught by experienced industry professionals, the course equips you with the creative confidence and technical tools to begin a career in animation or continue into the Bachelor of Creative Arts (Animation).','Animator, concept/character/environment artist, modeller, story writer, 3D or 2D animator, storyboard artist, rigger, compositor.','Animation, animation (2D), animation (3D), character design, compositing, concept art, concept development, creative process, digital art, digital sculpture, modelling (3D), motion capture, motion design, production art, professional + industry development, rendering, screen literacy, studio skills, traditional animation (2D), visual narrative, visual storytelling.','N/A','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/study-at-jmc/domestic-fees-financial-aid/','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/our-courses/animation/diploma-of-creative-arts-animation/'),
('773010','JMC','Bachelor of Creative Arts (Game Design)','The games industry is growing fast. In fact, the expertise and practices of game design and development is spilling over into a range of sectors, with design and development practices becoming widely adopted outside of purely gaming purposes.Game Design at JMC feeds this drive, providing the skills and knowledge to create fully immersive digital environments. Learn how to design, develop and implement an idea, with emphasis on creativity and expression through concept creation, digital drawing, environment modelling and game-engine implementation.Get the hands-on expertise with leading game industry development and production software, and use our 18-camera leading precision motion-capture suites and VR facilities needed to create interactive game prototypes and quality game assets. Graduate with the skills demanded by leading developers.You will be able to access the Full Adobe Creative Cloud Suite, Autodesk Maya, Wacom Intuos Pro + Cintiq tablets, Animation lightboxes, ball + socket stop-motion rigs, Dragonframe stop-motion software, 18-camera motion-capture suites, VR facilities, green-screen studios, renderers (Redshift, Pixar RenderMan, Arnold), Substance Painter for texturing, Zbrush for sculpting, Compositing tools (After Effects, Nuke), Katana for Look Development and Shotgun Studio for Project Planning + Management.With world class campuses in Sydney, Melbourne, and Brisbane, a dedicated team of academics and industry professional lecturers, and the opportunity to participate in international masterclasses and study abroad programs, JMC Academy is committed to ensuring our graduates make their own indelible mark on industry.All JMC bachelor degree graduates are eligible to apply for entry into JMC Academy&#39s Master of Creative Industries, or relevant post-grad qualifications at any Australian university.','Game designer/producer, creative director, concept/character/environment artist, modeller, technical director, story writer, production manager, 3D or 2D animator, storyboard artist, rigger, compositor. ','Art history, art and animation history, character modelling, character design (2D), clay sculpture, colour and design, concept art, concept development, digital sculpture, digital concept art, drawing, environment design (2D), figure modelling, game design, game studies, game asset creation (3D), game engine scripting (programming), game production, game-play mechanics, interactive multimedia, level design (games), motion capture, motion graphics, pixel art, production (games), prototyping, rendering, scriptwriting, sprite animation (2D), studio skills, user interface design (games). ','At JMC we have a dedicated Internship Program as well as work placement opportunities designed to have students apply their learning and gain hands-on experience in real industry roles. ','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/study-at-jmc/domestic-fees-financial-aid/','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/our-courses/game-design/bachelor-of-creative-arts-game-design/'),
('773011','JMC','Diploma of Creative Arts (Game Design)','The video game industry is growing fast. In fact, the expertise and practices of game design + development is spilling over into a range of sectors, with design and development practices becoming widely adopted outside of purely gaming purposes.\nJMC Academy’s Diploma of Game Design allows you to explore everything from concept drawing, digital sculpting and visual narrative to expressive animation techniques, game art development, 3D modelling, asset creation and building immersive game spaces. You will begin to understand the core components of visual narrative and games design and will adopt a range of rich, diverse and expressive animation techniques, which you’ll develop into sophisticated outcomes. A solid foundation in game-art development practice will provide you with the perfect platform upon which to deepen your critical level of knowledge and understanding in a Bachelor degree.','Game designer, concept/character/environment artist, modeller, story writer, production co-ordinator, 3D or 2D animator, storyboard artist, rigger, compositor, quality assurance tester.','Art History, art and animation history, character modeling, character design (2D), clay sculpture, colour and design, concept art, concept development, digital sculpture, digital concept art, drawing, environment design (2D), figure modelling, game design, game studies, game asset creation (3D), game engine scripting [programming], game production, game-play mechanics, interactive multimedia, level design (games), motion capture, motion graphics, pixel art, production (games), prototyping, rendering, scriptwriting, sprite animation (2D), studio skills, user interface design (games).','Students workshop and perform original songs from the outset, receiving feedback from industry professionals and collaborating across JMC’s creative disciplines in real-world project settings.','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/study-at-jmc/domestic-fees-financial-aid/','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/our-courses/game-design/diploma-of-creative-arts-game-design/'),
('773012','JMC','Bachelor of Creative Arts (Film and Television)','The world just can’t get enough of the magic of the moving image, and the global uptake of digital technology is creating unprecedented demand for professional content creators.From producers to directors, cinematographers, scriptwriters, motion graphics designers, editors and more, entertainment production is big business. Film and TV at JMC Academy is a hands-on production-based course that will give you the knowledge and the creative, technical and managerial skills to create and produce leading content for film, TV, live broadcasts, documentaries, commercials and music videos.Develop your creative expression and technical skills whilst mastering screenwriting, directing, cinematography, motion graphics and post-production, to launch your creative career.We take film and TV seriously at JMC, with studios full of the best tech in the trade. You’ll have access to highly sophisticated equipment and recording studios, including RED EPIC-W™ HELIUM™ 8K, Arri Amira series and Blackmagic Design Ursa Broadcast G2 cameras, green-screen studios, editing suites, colour grading equipment including powerful iMac Pros and Blackmagic Design DaVinci Resolve, a cinema/theatre fitted with 5.1 surround sound and full student loan facilities with lenses, cameras, lights and sound equipment available.With world class campuses in Sydney, Melbourne, and Brisbane, a dedicated team of academics and industry professional lecturers, and the opportunity to participate in international masterclasses and study abroad programs, JMC Academy is committed to ensuring our graduates make their own indelible mark on industry.All JMC, bachelor degree graduates are eligible to apply for entry into JMC Academy&#39s Master of Creative Industries, or relevant post-grad qualifications at any Australian university.','Director, cinematographer, scriptwriter, editor, producer, production manager, post-production supervisor, technical director, motion graphics designer, lighting designer, sound recordist, camera operator.','Broadcasting, camera operation, camera and lighting, cinematography, directing (film), directing (television), documentary production, film audio, film composition, film editing, filmmaking, industry and professional development, international cinema, lighting design, span \"background- (31, 31, 31)\"mise en scène, motion graphics, multi-cam broadcasting, music videos, popular culture, postproduction, producing (film), producing (television), screen history, screen and genre studies, screenwriting, short films, sound design, sound recording and design, television broadcasting, television studio production.','At JMC we have a dedicated Internship Program as well as work placement opportunities designed to have students apply their learning and gain hands-on experience in real industry roles.','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/study-at-jmc/domestic-fees-financial-aid/','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/our-courses/film-television-production/bachelor-of-creative-arts-film-television/'),
('773013','JMC','Diploma of Film and Television','As an introduction to the fundamentals of film and TV, the Diploma of Film and Television Production will let you explore cinematography, editing, lighting, location, sound recording, sound design, screenwriting and production management, providing you with the introductory knowledge and skills to move into entry level roles with the film and TV industry. Gain hands-on skills and professional insights crewing on an industry production and even produce your own documentary.\nWe take film and TV seriously at JMC, with studios full of the best tech in the trade. You’ll have access to our brand-new on-campus film and TV studio fitted out with highly sophisticated equipment, including Blackmagic Design Ursa Broadcast G2 cameras, and a green-screen. Additionally on our new Melbourne campus, you will access JMC’s editing suites, colour grading room including powerful iMac Pros and Blackmagic Design DaVinci Resolve, a cinema/theatre fitted with 5.1 surround sound and full student loan facilities with lenses, cameras, lights and sound equipment available. ','Director, cinematographer, scriptwriter, editor, producer, production manager, post-production supervisor, technical director, motion graphics designer, lighting designer, sound recordist, camera operator.','Broadcasting, camera operation, camera and lighting, cinematography, directing (film), directing (television), documentary production, film audio, film composition, film editing, filmmaking, industry and professional development, international cinema, lighting design, span \"background- (31, 31, 31)\"mise en scène, motion graphics, multi-cam broadcasting, music videos, popular culture, postproduction, producing (film), producing (television), screen history, screen and genre studies, screenwriting, short films, sound design, sound recording and design, television broadcasting, television studio production.','Students workshop and perform original songs from the outset, receiving feedback from industry professionals and collaborating across JMC’s creative disciplines in real-world project settings.','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/study-at-jmc/domestic-fees-financial-aid/','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/our-courses/film-television-production/diploma-of-film-television/'),
('773014','JMC','Bachelor of Design (Visual Communications)','The a href=\"https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/study-at-jmc/scholarships/\" \"noopener noreferrer\" \"_blank\"JMC Academy Design Scholarship supports eligible students commencing the Bachelor of Design (Visual Communication). The Scholarship provides a 30% tuition fee reduction for the full-time duration of the program.Technology is moving fast, and society is changing with it. If you’re passionate about all things design and the impact design has on people and culture, this course is for you.JMC Academy’s Bachelor of Design (Visual Communication) helps you to explore the fundamentals of graphic design and the technical skills required to create aesthetically appealing messaging. Through this course, you will delve into the design process, from research, ideation, sketching and prototyping, to implementation and watch your work come to life.JMC Academy understands how creative people learn. Removed from traditional classroom learning, you’ll enjoy working within a design-studio environment. You will gain experience tackling creative briefs, sketching ideas and creating quick prototypes for testing with a realised digital outcome. You will learn the processes involved with creating compelling user experiences, and utilise different tools and tech to help you make it.We take design seriously at JMC. Our classes are full of the best tech in the trade, constantly updated with industry-standard tech and the latest software out there. From day one, you’ll attend classes set up in studio-like environments and have access to a range of equipment including Wacom graphics tablets, HTC Vive VR tech, and DSLR cameras that will allow you to experiment and design to your heart’s desire. You’ll also receive a complimentary Adobe Creative Cloud licence.With world class campuses in Sydney, Melbourne and Brisbane, a dedicated team of academics and industry professional lecturers, and the opportunity to participate in international masterclasses and study abroad programs, JMC Academy is committed to ensuring our graduates make their own indelible mark on industry.All JMC bachelor degree graduates are eligible to apply for entry into JMC Academy&#39s Master of Creative Industries, or relevant post-grad qualification at any Australian university.','Experience designer, UX consultant/designer, graphic designer, art director, social media designer, content coordinator, web/app designer, 3D visualiser, motion designer.','3D design, communication, creative arts, design, design photography, design theory, digital design, digital imaging, graphic design, information design, information technology, interactive design, story telling, typography, user experience design, visual communication. ','At JMC we have a dedicated Internship Program as well as work placement opportunities designed to have students apply their learning and gain hands-on experience in real industry roles. ','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/study-at-jmc/domestic-fees-financial-aid/','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/our-courses/design-visual-communication/bachelor-of-design-visual-communication/'),
('773015','JMC','Diploma of Design (Visual Communication)','Technology is moving fast, and society is changing with it. If you’re passionate about the impact design has on people and culture, this course is for you.\nJMC Academy’s Diploma of Design (Visual Communication) helps you to explore the fundamentals of graphic design and introduces you to the technical skills required to create aesthetically appealing messaging. Through this course, you will delve into the design process, from research, ideation, sketching and prototyping, to implementation and watch your work come to life.\nJMC understand how creative people learn. Removed from traditional classroom learning, you’ll enjoy working within a design-studio environment. You will gain knowledge in how to tackle a brief, sketching ideas and creating quick prototypes for testing. You will learn the processes involved with creating compelling user experiences, and utilise different tools and tech to help you make it.','Experience designer, UX consultant/designer, graphic designer, art director, social media designer, content coordinator, web/app designer, 3D visualiser, motion designer.','3D design, communication, creative arts, design, design photography, design theory, digital design, digital imaging, graphic design, information design, information technology, interactive design, story telling, typography, user experience design, visual communication.','N/A','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/study-at-jmc/domestic-fees-financial-aid/','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/our-courses/design-visual-communication/diploma-of-design-visual-communication/'),
('773016','JMC','Bachelor of Music with major in Music Production','Music technology has shifted the possibilities of how songwriters and composers create, and the JMC Music Production course enables creatives to work in a practical way, focusing on core musicianship skills and industry-standard DAW platforms to create and produce your own music. The music production major is focused on the use of technology as a musical tool and encourages the adaptation of new technologies, and incorporation of new software, hardware, and other media alongside your music. \nAt JMC Academy, our Music Production course is designed around practical projects, with a strong focus on individual musicianship and developing a personal artistic style. With connections to APRA AMCOS and exchange programs globally, this course ensures you are able to develop critical business skills alongside your practice to launch your dream career. Whether you want to make it as a DJ, Producer or Composer, we’ve got you covered. \nGetting some time in the studio is a crucial part of your study at JMC and during the course, you’ll be working with live and virtual instruments to craft your music. Designed for recording high-quality live performances, our songwriting suites and production studios feature ProTools, Logic, Ableton Live and Native Instruments, along with a variety of MIDI controllers, synthesisers, and top of the range microphones. \nMusic Production at JMC is one of 3 majors offered under the Bachelor of Music. Other major areas include: \n \n contemporary performance songwriting  \n music production.  \n\nWith world class campuses in Sydney, Melbourne and Brisbane, a dedicated team of academics and industry professional lecturers, and the opportunity to participate in international masterclasses, music and songwriting camps and study abroad programs, JMC Academy is committed to ensuring our graduates make their own indelible mark on industry. \nExtend your studies with our new double degree! JMC Academy’s Bachelor of Music and Bachelor of Entertainment Business Management offers you a new way to pair technical and creative skills in music with the essential business know-how required to understand all facets of the music business industry. This unique blend of artistry and business acumen equips students with the skills to successfully manage their own career and transform their music into a marketable product. \nAll JMC bachelor degree graduates are eligible to apply for entry into JMC Academy’s Master of Creative Industries, or relevant post-grad qualifications at any Australian university.','Music producer, film and TV composer, resident/staff writer, advertising creative (jingle writer), music publisher, music teacher, electronic music artist, label manager, sound designer, recording artist. ','Arranging and orchestration, collaborative recording, composition techniques, ear training, ensemble, history of popular music, history of western music, lyrical influences, lyrics and songwriting, music business, music cultures, music production studies, music technology, music theory, music and media, performing and creating with Ableton Live, production, screen sound and music, songwriting and arranging, tutoring techniques.','At JMC we have a dedicated Internship Program as well as work placement opportunities designed to have students apply their learning and gain hands-on experience in real industry roles. ','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/study-at-jmc/domestic-fees-financial-aid/','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/our-courses/music-production/bachelor-of-music-with-major-in-music-production/'),
('773017','JMC','Diploma of Music with major in Music Production','The Diploma of Music with major in Music Production at JMC Academy is a practical, 8-month course that equips aspiring producers, composers and beatmakers with the foundational skills to create and produce original music across styles and platforms.\nFrom your first trimester, you’ll dive into studio sessions using professional DAWs like ProTools, Logic, Ableton Live and Native Instruments, gaining hands-on experience with both live and virtual instruments. With a strong focus on musicianship, studio workflow and personal artistic development, this course prepares you to turn musical ideas into fully produced tracks.\nYou’ll also learn how to adapt to evolving technology and start building the business and collaborative skills needed to thrive in today’s music and media industries.','Music producer, film and TV composer, resident/staff writer, advertising creative (jingle writer), music publisher, music teacher, electronic music artist, label manager, sound designer, recording artist.','Digital audio workstations (DAWs), music production techniques, studio workflow, MIDI sequencing, sound design, recording and mixing, music theory and musicianship, songwriting fundamentals, and collaboration with artists across performance and songwriting.','Students workshop and perform original songs from the outset, receiving feedback from industry professionals and collaborating across JMC’s creative disciplines in real-world project settings.','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/study-at-jmc/domestic-fees-financial-aid/','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/our-courses/music-production/diploma-of-music-with-major-in-music-production/?utm_campaign=Sep2025IntakeAds&utm_source=Google+Paid&utm_content=search&utm_campus=sydney&utm_course=generic&gclid=EAIaIQobChMI85rT8e7HjwMVQqNmAh15jS1_EAAYASAAEgLUGPD_BwE'),
('773018','JMC','Bachelor of Creative Arts (Acting)','Acting at JMC Academy provides an exciting and immersive pathway into your professional career as an actor for film, theatre, television and new media. Our program will prepare you to pursue a professional and sustainable career in performance - preparing not only the actor’s knowledge and skill base but also the actor’s process to meet the specific needs and nuances in this changing and diversifying performing arts industry. \nOur Bachelor of Creative Arts (Acting) will nurture talent and performance craft, whilst supporting the creation of new ideas, projects and creative ventures, ensuring our graduates are able to fully and confidently participate with personal leadership in all facets of their industry. \nJMC take practical experience seriously, throughout the duration of your studies, gain a wide range of performance experience across stage, screen and new media including animation and game design in collaboration with students from across JMC’s creative disciplines including working on our very own Film Student productions Then take your skills beyond our advanced design campus and perform in fully staged productions at some of Sydney’s best theatre spaces including Belvoir St Theatre and the Sydney Opera House. \nWith world class campuses in Sydney, Melbourne and Brisbane, a dedicated team of academics and industry professional lecturers, and the opportunity to participate in international masterclasses and study abroad programs, JMC Academy is committed to ensuring our graduates make their own indelible mark on industry. \nJMC Actors graduate with a complete graduation package including a professional showreel, industry showcase and head-shots ready for us (and you!) to share with industry. All JMC bachelor degree graduates are eligible to apply for entry into JMC Academy’s Master of Creative Industries, or relevant post-grad qualifications at any Australian university. ','Actor, film actor, television actor, theatre actor, voice-over artist for film or radio, computer-generated (CGI) or animation character actor, motion-capture actor, music theatre performer, television commercial actor, live entertainment performer. ','Acting, acting career, acting techniques, acting for film, acting for new media, acting for stage, acting for television, devised theatre, drama, entrepreneurship, filmmaking, heightened language, heightened voice, improvisation, internship, musical theatre, performance, performing arts, professional practice, theatre, voice and movement. ','N/A','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/study-at-jmc/domestic-fees-financial-aid/','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/our-courses/acting/bachelor-of-creative-arts-acting/'),
('773019','JMC','Diploma of Creative Arts (Acting)','The Acting Diploma at JMC equips students with the underpinning skills and knowledge to apply the foundation acting principles to a performance, to develop creative and collaborative performance concepts and provides the necessary educational and academic framework to enable further study.\nThe Diploma comprises of the first two trimesters of our Acting Degree program, providing an exit point for students wishing to develop the introductory skills of acting as a pathway for further learning. The highly practical course allows you to gain an introductory level of a wide range of performance skills – and put them into practice across both stage and screen.','Actor, film actor, television actor, theatre actor, voice-over artist for film or radio, commercial actor.','Acting techniques, acting for film, acting for stage, acting for television, drama, heightened language, heightened voice, musical theatre, performing arts, theatre, voice and movement.','N/A','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/study-at-jmc/domestic-fees-financial-aid/','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/our-courses/animation/diploma-of-creative-arts-animation/'),
('773020','JMC','Bachelor of Creative Arts (Acting) with major in Music Theatre','This hands-on degree trains you across the three core disciplines of music theatre: acting, singing, and dance. You’ll build your craft in an environment that mirrors industry standards, with intensive studio practice, performance-based projects, and mentorship from experienced creatives working in theatre, film, and TV.\nFrom classic musicals to contemporary works and screen performance, you’ll develop the versatility needed to thrive on any stage or set. You’ll collaborate with students across JMC’s creative disciplines, working with filmmakers, designers and audio engineers to bring full productions to life, and gain real-world experience through public performances, showcases, and internships.','Music theatre performer, stage or screen actor, vocalist, voiceover artist, dance/theatre teacher, live entertainment performer, devised theatre artist, touring artist, entertainment creative. ','Acting for stage, ballet, broadway jazz, career sustainability, commercial dance, ensemble voice, entrepreneurship, musicianship, private vocal lessons, screen and new media, tap.','Regular public performances and fully staged musicals, live showcases at professional venues, tv and film performance experience, gain experience in voice over and motion capture performance, cross-disciplinary collaboration with film, audio, and design students, final-year showcase and professional portfolio including showreel and headshots.','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/study-at-jmc/domestic-fees-financial-aid/','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/our-courses/music-theatre/bachelor-of-creative-arts-acting-with-major-in-music-theatre/'),
('773021','JMC','Diploma of Creative Arts (Acting) with major in Music Theatre','This eight month diploma is designed to give you a practical introduction to the core disciplines of music theatre, acting, singing, and dance, within a creative, industry-informed environment. You’ll develop your performance skills through regular classes, performance projects, and showcases, while building confidence and technique across stage and screen.\nThroughout your studies, you’ll work closely with experienced performers and teachers, and collaborate with students from other creative disciplines including Film and Audio. Whether you’re preparing for further study or seeking to launch your career, this course lays a strong foundation for life in the performing arts.','Emerging music theatre performer, stage or screen actor, vocalist, voiceover artist, ensemble artist, live entertainer, performer-in-training, performing arts facilitator.','Acting, dance, musicianship, professional practice, voice and movement.','N/A','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/study-at-jmc/domestic-fees-financial-aid/','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/our-courses/acting/diploma-of-creative-arts-acting/'),
('773022','JMC','Bachelor of Creative Technology (Audio Engineering and Sound Production) &amp Bachelor of Entertainment Business Management','This unique double degree is built for future audio professionals who want to do more than just work behind the desk. You’ll gain the technical skills to record, mix and produce sound at a professional level, while also learning how to navigate the business side of the entertainment industry with additional units in artist management, marketing, events, contracts, and more.\nWhether you’re interested in live events, studio recording, post-production or freelance work, this course equips you to become an industry ready Audio Engineer emand/em gain the skills to build a sustainable creative career. You’ll get access to some of the best audio tech in the country and learn from experienced lecturers who know the industry inside-out.','Audio engineer, sound designer, live sound technician, studio manager, music producer, tour manager, artist manager, events or festival producer, entertainment entrepreneur, label assistant or A&ampR coordinator.','Acoustic design, audio engineering, AV, digital audio workstation, immersive audio, live event production, live sound, mixing techniques, music business, music production, post production audio, sound design, sound for screen, studio sound.','Hands-on training in world-class recording studios and live sound environments, access to professional audio gear and software from day one, internship opportunities with studios, festivals, events companies and more, real-world projects including audio for film, games, and media, cross-disciplinary collaboration with film and music students.','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/study-at-jmc/domestic-fees-financial-aid/','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/our-courses/'),
('773023','JMC','Bachelor of Music and Bachelor of Entertainment Business Management','This double degree is designed for musicians who want to take creative control of their future. You’ll hone your skills in performance, songwriting, or music production, while also learning how to manage your brand, release your work, and run the business side of your career.\nWith this unique combo of artistry and entrepreneurial skills, you’ll be equipped to launch original projects, build a fanbase, and make confident moves in an ever-evolving music industry. Study includes studio time, business planning, project management, copyright law, marketing, and plenty of opportunities to collaborate and perform.','Recording artist, songwriter, producer, band manager, label assistant, booking agent, digital marketer, music publisher, music business entrepreneur, A&ampR rep.','Arranging and orchestration, business planning, composition, copyright and publishing, deal making, development (A&ampR), digital commerce, ear training, entertainment business finance, entrepreneurship, festival management, internship, marketing, music and media, music business, music production, music theory, music, musicianship, public relations, screen sound, talent discovery, talent management, tour management, tutoring techniques.','Studio-based learning and access to professional music production tools, Live performance opportunities on and off campus, Internships with labels, publishers, festivals or media companies, Release original music and develop a professional portfolio, Build your brand through marketing, digital strategy and audience development.','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/study-at-jmc/domestic-fees-financial-aid/','https://www.jmcacademy.edu.au/our-courses/music-entertainment-business/bachelor-of-music-bachelor-of-entertainment-business-management/'),
('785000','UON','Bachelor of Medical Science and Doctor of Medicine (Joint Medical Program)','The Bachelor of Medical Science and Doctor of Medicine (Joint Medical Program) is offered jointly by the University of Newcastle and University of New England in partnership with Hunter New England and Central Coast Local Health Districts. There is a common curriculum across both campuses. The five-year program provides students with the knowledge and skills to commence a career as a doctor, able to provide and improve individual and community healthcare in an Australian context and internationally. The program is taught by expert clinicians and researchers actively involved in new research discoveries. Advanced simulated learning environments and educational technologies ensure access to the latest resources in medical education.The program is responsive to a rapidly changing health environment. The structure and content are designed and reviewed by a multidisciplinary team of specialist doctors, healthcare clinicians, health service experts, medical educators, and student representatives. The primary intent of the program is to develop work-ready graduates that enter internship with a dedication to excellence in patient care and a commitment to lifelong learning.Applicants successful in gaining entry to this program will be offered a place at the University of Newcastle or University of New England. Consideration is given to the enrolment location preference on the applicant’s JMP direct online university application. There is no guarantee that candidates will be allocated their preferred location. Applicants who gain entry to the University of Newcastle may express a preference on their JMP direct online university application to commence the program at the Central Coast Clinical School.Students enrolled in this program are required to undertake clinical placements at locations away from their university of enrolment. These placements may be outside the standard university semester dates. In third, fourth and fifth years, clinical placements are completed within the six JMP clinical schools. Students will have the opportunity to select, or may be required, to be located at a rural clinical school (Armidale/Taree/Tamworth) for one year of study. All students are expected to complete one year at a metropolitan clinical school (Hunter/Central Coast/Maitland), unless an exception is granted.This degree requires students to participate in clinical placements in NSW Health facilities. During placements, students will be subject to policies and procedures laid down by NSW Health. Students must also meet all NSW Health verification requirements before attending. Students enrolling in this degree are required to obtain a WorkCover-approved Provide First Aid Certificate during semester one.Prospective students will be required to perform all aspects of medical practices, including physical examination and routine medical and surgical procedures, to meet program requirements. Students may be required to practice hands-on examinations and simulated treatments/procedures with other students in laboratory classes. a href=\"https://www.newcastle.edu.au/joint-medical-program/inherent-requirements\" \"noopener noreferrer\" \"_blank\"For more information refer to Inherent Requirements.Applicants who may be unsure of their ability to complete the program and work in the profession should contact the University prior to applying.','span \"background- color: windowtext\"There are many career pathways to follow with further post-graduate study: Addiction medicine, Anaesthetics, Clinical genetics, Dermatology, Emergency medicine, General practice, Intensive care medicine, Medical administration, Obstetrics &amp Gynaecology, Occupational &amp Environmental medicine, Ophthalmology, Paediatrics &amp child health, Pain medicine, Palliative medicine, Pathology, Physician (general and specialist), Psychiatry, Public health medicine, Radiation oncology, Radiology &amp nuclear medicine, Rehabilitation medicine, Rural and Remote medicine, Sexual health medicine, Sports and exercise medicine, and Surgery (general and specialist). ','Medicine, including medical sciences, clinical medical and surgical specialties (e.g., respiratory and cardiovascular medicine, cancer treatment, orthopaedics), community and public health, women’s and children’s health, mental health, hospital-based medicine, research and the critical evaluation of evidence. ','span \"color: windowtext : transparent\"Clinical experience: clinical experience can begin in the first year of study and greatly increases throughout the five years. Students will gain a range of professional experiences as they meet with patients in general practice facilities, hospital wards and outpatient clinics, while they spend time with doctors and their teams. Students will have the opportunity to gain hands-on experience in the delivery of healthcare using the latest emerging technologies. span \"color: windowtext : transparent\"Specialty placements: in the final two years of study, students undertake specialty placements in general practice, women’s &amp children’s health, mental health, general medicine, surgery &amp trauma, intensive care, anaesthetics and emergency medicine. Our extensive network enables field experiences in urban, rural, and regional settings in Australia and elective study overseas. ','https://www.newcastle.edu.au/current-students/study-essentials/fees-scholarships','https://www.newcastle.edu.au/joint-medical-program'),
('785000_JC','UNE','Bachelor of Medical Science and Doctor of Medicine (Joint Medical Program)','The Bachelor of Medical Science and Doctor of Medicine (Joint Medical Program) is offered jointly by the University of Newcastle and University of New England in partnership with Hunter New England and Central Coast Local Health Districts. There is a common curriculum across both campuses. The five-year program provides students with the knowledge and skills to commence a career as a doctor, able to provide and improve individual and community healthcare in an Australian context and internationally. \nThe program is taught by expert clinicians and researchers actively involved in breaking research discoveries. Advanced simulated learning environments and educational technologies ensure access to the latest resources in medical education.\nThe program is responsive to a rapidly changing health environment. The structure and content are designed and reviewed by a multidisciplinary team of specialist doctors, healthcare clinicians, health service experts, medical educators, and student representatives. The primary intent of the program is to develop work-ready graduates that enter internship with a dedication to excellence in patient care and a commitment to lifelong learning.\nApplicants successful in gaining entry to this program will be offered a place at the University of Newcastle or University of New England. Consideration is given to the enrolment location preference on the applicant’s JMP direct online university application. There is no guarantee that candidates will be allocated their preferred location. Applicants who gain entry to the University of Newcastle may express a preference on their JMP direct online university application to commence the program at the Central Coast Clinical School.\nStudents enrolled in this program are required to undertake clinical placements at locations away from their university of enrolment. These placements may be outside the standard university semester dates. In third, fourth and fifth years, clinical placements are completed within the six JMP clinical schools. Students will have the opportunity to select, or may be required, to be located at a rural clinical school (Armidale/Taree/Tamworth) for one year of study. All students are required to complete one year at a metropolitan clinical school (Hunter/Central Coast/Maitland).\nThis degree requires students to participate in clinical placements in NSW Health facilities. During placements, students will be subject to policies and procedures laid down by NSW Health. Students must also meet all NSW Health verification requirements before attending. Students enrolling in this degree are required to obtain a WorkCover-approved Provide First Aid Certificate during semester one those students enrolling at the University of New England are also required to obtain a Working with Children Check.\nProspective students will be required to perform all aspects of medical practices, including physical examination and routine medical and surgical procedures, to meet program requirements. Students may be required to practice hands-on examinations and simulated treatments/procedures with other students in laboratory classes. \na href=\"https://www.newcastle.edu.au/joint-medical-program/inherent-requirements\" \"_blank\"For more information refer to Inherent Requirements.\nApplicants who may be unsure of their ability to complete the program and work in the profession should contact the University prior to applying. ','There are many career pathways to follow with further post-graduate study: Addiction medicine, Anaesthetics, Clinical genetics, Dermatology, Emergency medicine, General practice, Intensive care medicine, Medical administration, Obstetrics & Gynaecology, Occupational & Environmental medicine, Ophthalmology, Paediatrics & child health, Pain medicine, Palliative medicine, Pathology, Physician (general and specialist), Psychiatry, Public health medicine, Radiation oncology, Radiology & nuclear medicine, Rehabilitation medicine, Rural and Remote medicine, Sexual health medicine, Sports and exercise medicine, and Surgery (general and specialist).\n','The program includes clinical exposure from early in the first semester. Areas of study during the five-year program include medical sciences, clinical medical and surgical specialties, women’s and children’s health, mental health, hospital-based medicine, general practice, community and public health, research skills and the critical evaluation of evidence. There is opportunity to preference a pathway to personalise your degree and to complete a substantial research project. The fifth year of study is themed ‘transition to practice’ and is focused on an immersive clinical experience in medicine, surgery, and critical care, in preparation for internship.\n','The JMP delivers opportunity for placements in urban, regional, and rural settings across Australia. Our clinical teachers are highly skilled national and international experts in their fields. Clinical experience begins in the first semester and culminates in an immersive clinical experience in the final year. A range of professional experiences and teaching from practicing doctors is central to the program, as medical students develop an in-depth understanding of the patient journey through encounters with patients and carers in hospital wards, outpatient clinics, and in the community. There is opportunity to develop an understanding of global health systems and to undertake clinical placements and exchanges overseas. The program may be personalised by preferencing a pathway of interest and completing a research project during third, fourth and fifth years. \n','NULL','https://www.une.edu.au/study/courses/bachelor-of-medical-science-and-doctor-of-medicine'),
('79','AMPA_AD','Associate Degree of Music (Performance)','AMPA’s Associate Degree of Music (Performance) is an advanced diploma level (AQF level 6) qualification. It covers the same content as stages 1-3 of AMPA’s a href=\"https://uac.edu.au/undergraduate/courses/apply-direct/ampa/80.shtml\" \"_blank\" Bachelor of Music (Performance) with the addition of a foundational stage at the start of the course, stage A. It is a highly practical course, personalised to the individual requirements and interests of each student. Students may undertake a range of units and choose from an array of electives to complement their major studies and subsequently diversify their skill sets.\nAMPA’s music degrees merge high-level performance and practical training with academic rigour and unparalleled industry insight. Students can personalise their degree based around their individual interests and aspirations. AMPA undergrads may choose to undertake a second instrument or vocal study and focus on two performance areas (such as singing and songwriting, voice and keyboard, guitar and bass, violin and viola). The possibilities are endless and are designed to enhance graduate career outcomes. Students may also choose electives across all areas to further tailor their degree.\nThe Associate Degree of Music (Performance) is a nested award into the Bachelor of Music (Performance). Students who successfully complete the first four trimesters of the Associate Degree of Music (Performance) are eligible to transfer into the Bachelor of Music (Performance) and graduate with both awards.','emPerformance:/em Performer in professional orchestras and bands, recording artist, session musician, stage producer, stage manager, conductor, composer/arranger, opera and ballet.emAdvertising:/em Specialist performer, musical director, producer, jingle writer, sourcing and sampling music.emRadio, film/television and digital media:/em Music video specialist, composer/arranger of film and radio scores, soundtrack producer, music for games, music director, music promoter, editor, copyright and contract administrator, voiceover specialist, and sourcing personnel.emMusic teaching:/em Teaching in government, Catholic and independent schools, TAFE, universities and higher education providers (with further study), music studios and private music tuition. Further postgraduate qualifications in education/teaching will be required for secondary teaching positions.emEvents:/em Manager, composer, programmer, promoter and distributor, presenter and marketing manager.emMusic media:/em Music journalist, music critic, composer and arranger, researcher, producer, scriptwriter, on-air presenter and commentator.\n',' Classical performance, composition, contemporary performance, jazz performance, musical theatre, production.\n','N/A','NULL','https://ampa.edu.au/contemporary-music/'),
('80','AMPA_AD','Bachelor of Music (Performance)','AMPA’s Bachelor of Music degree is a highly practical course, personalised to the individual requirements and interests of each student. Students may undertake a range of units and choose from an array of electives to complement their major studies and subsequently diversify their skill sets.\nAMPA’s music degrees merge high-level performance and practical training with academic rigour and unparalleled industry insight. Students can personalise their degree based around their individual interests and aspirations. AMPA undergrads may choose to undertake a second instrument or vocal study and focus on two performance areas (such as singing and songwriting, voice and keyboard, guitar and bass, violin and viola). The possibilities are endless and are designed to enhance graduate career outcomes. Students may also choose electives across all areas to further tailor their degree. \nStudents who successfully complete the first four trimesters of Bachelor of Music are eligible to graduate with an AssocDeg Music (Performance). ',' emPerformance:/em Performer in professional orchestras and bands, recording artist, session musician, stage producer, stage manager, conductor, composer/arranger, opera and ballet.emAdvertising:/em Specialist performer, musical director, producer, jingle writer, sourcing and sampling music.emRadio, film/television and digital media:/em Music video specialist, composer/arranger of film and radio scores, soundtrack producer, music for games, music director, music promoter, editor, copyright and contract administrator, voiceover specialist, and sourcing personnel.emMusic teaching:/em Teaching in government, Catholic and independent schools, TAFE, universities and higher education providers (with further study), music studios and private music tuition. Further postgraduate qualifications in education/teaching will be required for secondary teaching positions.emEvents:/em Manager, composer, programmer, promoter and distributor, presenter and marketing manager.emMusic media:/em Music journalist, music critic, composer and arranger, researcher, producer, scriptwriter, on-air presenter and commentator.\n',' Classical performance, composition, contemporary performance, jazz performance, musical theatre, production.\n','N/A','NULL','http://www.ampa.edu.au/'),
('CRS1300157','ACHW_AD','Bachelor of Applied Health Science (Clinical Aesthetics)','The Bachelor of Applied Health Science (Clinical Aesthetics) is the highest qualification in Higher Education available in Australia to prepare you for a career in the dynamic fields of Dermal Therapy and Clinical Aesthetics. This three-year degree will equip you with an advanced level of knowledge and skills to combine science with clinical practice, giving you the confidence to work with clients and medical health professionals.\nThis degree is divided into four streams:\n \n Human Biosciences \n Applied Health Science \n Health Communication and Management \n Clinical Aesthetics Practice\n\nIn your first year of study, you will be introduced to the fundamentals of professional and clinical practice while learning about skin and the integumentary system, human structure and function, and dermal therapy techniques. You will progress to more advanced subjects in your second year, such as learning about differential diagnoses in skin disorders, the chemistry of cosmetics, and advanced dermal interventions. The final year of study examines the relationships between psychology, stress, and ageing and teaches you about perioperative skin care and clinical observation techniques.\nIn the practical clinics of the Bachelor of Applied Health Science (Clinical Aesthetics), you will gain hands-on experience with the following treatments, technologies, and modalities:\n \n Microdermabrasion \n Hydrodermabrasion \n Chemical Peels \n Laser/IPL Hair Reduction \n Skin Needling \n Laser Tattoo Removal \n Laser/IPL for Pigmentation and Vascular Removal \n Plasma Pen Technology \n Electrical Facial Treatments \n Manual Lymphatic Drainage\n\nThis degree is delivered in a hybrid model of online learning and authentic clinic experience. This unique delivery mode ensures you can balance your study with the other commitments you have in your life. Learn the theory of dermal therapy and health science through our online learning platform, before attending dedicated clinic blocks that provide hands-on expertise with real clients.\nNote: Practical clinics are located in Melbourne, Sydney, and the Gold Coast.\n\n','With a strong theoretical understanding and practical experience, graduating from this degree will enable you for work in the Clinical Aesthetics industry. You will be equipped to own and operate your own clinic or work in Laser and Dermal Therapy Clinics, Wellness and Healthy Ageing, Dermatology, Cosmetic Research and Development, and Cosmetic Medicine and Surgery Clinics.\n',' Dermal therapy, human biosciences, integumentary system, light-based technology, clinical aesthetics, cosmetic chemistry, clinical practice, anti-ageing, patho-physiology, skin disorder diagnosis, nutrition, perioperative skin care.\n','N/A','NULL','https://www.achw.edu.au/courses/bachelor-of-applied-health-science-clinical-aesthetics'),
('CRS1400148','ACHW_AD','Associate Degree in Applied Health Science (Dermal Therapy)','The Associate Degree in Applied Health Science (Dermal Therapy) is one of the highest qualification in Higher Education available in Australia to prepare you for a career in the dynamic field of Dermal Therapy. This two-year degree will equip you with an advanced level of knowledge and skills to combine science with clinical practice, helping you launch your career and providing you a step towards a Bachelor.\nThis degree is divided into four streams:\n \n Human Biosciences \n Applied Health Science \n Health Communication and Management \n Clinical Aesthetics Practice\n\nIn your first year of study, you will be introduced to the fundamentals of professional and clinical practice while learning about skin and the integumentary system, human structure and function, and dermal therapy techniques. You will progress to more advanced subjects in your second year, such as learning about differential diagnoses in skin disorders, the chemistry of cosmetics, and advanced dermal interventions. \nIn the practical clinics of the Associate Degree in Applied Health Science (Dermal Therapy), you will gain hands-on experience with the following treatments, technologies, and modalities:\n \n Microdermabrasion \n Hydrodermabrasion \n Chemical Peels \n Laser/IPL Hair Reduction \n Skin Needling \n Laser Tattoo Removal \n Laser/IPL for Pigmentation and Vascular Removal \n Plasma Pen Technology \n Electrical Facial Treatments \n Manual Lymphatic Drainage\n\nThis degree is delivered in a hybrid model of online learning and authentic clinic experience. This unique delivery mode ensures you can balance your study with the other commitments you have in your life. Learn the theory of dermal therapy and health science through our online learning platform, before attending dedicated clinic blocks that provide hands-on expertise with real clients.\nNote: Practical clinics are located in Melbourne, Sydney, and the Gold Coast.\n','With a strong theoretical understanding and practical experience, graduating from this degree will enable you for work in the Dermal Therapy industry. You will be equipped to own and operate your own clinic or work in Laser and Dermal Therapy Clinics, Wellness and Healthy Ageing, Dermatology, Cosmetic Research and Development, and Cosmetic Medicine and Surgery Clinics. \n','Dermal therapy, human biosciences, integumentary system, light-based technology, clinical aesthetics, cosmetic chemistry, clinical practice, anti-ageing, patho-physiology, skin disorder diagnosis, nutrition, perioperative skin care.\n','N/A','NULL','https://www.achw.edu.au/courses/associate-degree-in-applied-health-science-dermal-therapy'),
('CUA60620-FC','AIEAD_AD','Advanced Diploma of Screen and Media – Specialising in Filmmaking','AIE’s Advanced Diploma of Screen and Media – Specialising in Filmmaking – is a highly practical course designed to expand your visual storytelling and creative thinking. You will be trained by experienced industry practitioners in the exciting practice of filmmaking using the philosophy of learning by doing. \nWe replicate the real-world industry and operate like a production house. You are empowered to generate original ideas, develop and pitch your projects. Crews are formed and projects are realised from pre-production to shoot to post-production. It’s a fun, vibrant, hard-working environment where you can pursue projects that inspire you. Learn the art of collaboration by making short dramas, comedies, documentaries and music videos, incorporating the emerging technology of Virtual Production. You will work on a large volume of films in multiple crew roles and have your films screened publicly at the cinema at the end of each year. Having learnt writing, directing, producing, camera, audio and editing, you will be technically and creatively ready to work in traditional film roles.\nThis film course is the first in Australia to integrate Virtual Production technologies into a filmmaking course. The Virtual Production components of the course include pre-visualisation, virtual scouting techniques, and virtual production performance capture using real-time environments to ensure you will graduate with in-demand skills in this cutting-edge technology.\nYou will have access to the latest professional filmmaking equipment including Sony, Black Magic and Arri cameras, Arri anamorphic lenses, motion control dollies, mixers, microphones, props, sets, costumes and an LED wall virtual production studio at each campus. As well as professional editing and colour grading software. You will have the opportunity to build your network by collaborating with AIE’s visual effects students across AIE campuses.\nAIE’s Filmmaking course leverages the highly successful MAPS Film School Program, now acquired by AIE, which trained more than 1000 alumni and 1500 films over the past 35 years. Graduates have had their short films featured in film festivals around the world. Alumni can be found working all over Australia and the world and credited on blockbuster films and TV shows, including emSpider-man: No Way Home/em, emThe Lego Movies/em and emLoki/em as well as AIE’s funded and produced feature films such as emSissy/em, emThe Furies/em, emMe and My Mates/em and emthe Zombie Apocalypse/em and emBlue World Order/em.','Producer, director, virtual production producer, virtual production supervisor, camera operator, sound recorder, boom operator, editor, sound designer, runner, production assistant and assistant director. Graduates have established their own production houses as well as setting up as freelancers.\n','Storytelling, idea development, pitching, directing, producing, pre-visualisation, safety, managing locations, cinematography, recording sound, editing, colour grading, post audio, LED virtual volume film production and collaborating with visual effects departments. \n','Students develop hands-on skills and knowledge by working on real-world film projects with industry practitioners.\n','NULL','https://aie.edu.au/virtualproduction'),
('CUA60620-VC','AIEAD_AD','Advanced Diploma of Screen and Media – Specialising in 3D Animation and Visual Effects','Visual effects artists, animators and compositors create the fantastic worlds, superhuman feats and spectacular imagery that you see on the big (and small) screen. AIE’s 3D Animation and Visual Effects program runs over two years, full-time, and is designed to get you into these industries. It is a practical course designed to give the best technical training using the latest state-of-the-art technology.\nThis course has been written in consultation with leading film and visual effects studios, enabling you to complete impressive film projects that showcase your skills and create a professional showreel to impress potential employers. AIE graduates have worked on blockbuster films and TV shows, including emSpider-man: No Way Home/em, emThe Lego Movies/em and emLoki/em.','Animator, modeller, surfacing artist, lighting artist, technical artist, rigger (for animation), FX artist, compositor, matchmove artist, production coordinator.\n','3Modelling, texturing, look development, lighting, rigging, animation, compositing, effects and simulation, matchmove, production pipelines, production coordination, portfolio development, professional development. Many of these skills are mastered through a series of major projects that are focused on environment art, character art, character animation, visual effects and film production.A key area of study in this program is two production-focused projects where short animated films are developed collaboratively. Teams learn real-world production cycles in an industry-simulated development environment, from pitching their ideas to screening their finished work.\n',' AIE courses are taught in a studio-simulated learning environment. Students develop hands-on skills and knowledge by working on real-world tasks. AIE Trainers are experienced industry professionals who know what it takes to make it in animation and visual effects.\n','NULL','https://aie.edu.au/animate');
